window.MG_LAZY_DATA["data/lazy/courses/a173-de89bafb3eab0ac3.json"]={sha256:"de89bafb3eab0ac3d11b59429de020bf30fc260279c14d529036f2f2130d1ca1",value:{"id":"a173","title":"半導體光放大器整合","titleEn":"Semiconductor optical-amplifier integration","category":"packaging","kind":"course","summary":"從增益壓縮、自發輻射與光電熱介面拆成 4 階段、24 項可保存的工程作業；包含物理模型、算例、可區分失效的量測與驗收證據。","summaryEn":"Four stages and 24 saveable work packages investigate gain compression, spontaneous emission and optoelectrothermal interfaces, including physical models, a worked example, discriminating measurements and acceptance evidence.","sourceIds":["v9c-soaexperiment","v9c-mprint","v10-video-ea6d9da34f55"],"status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","curriculumVersion":9,"depth":4,"stepCount":24,"estimatedMinutes":840,"simulationOnly":true,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"subcategory":"pkg-sources","scope":"公開原理的概念設計與資料判讀課，非供應商配方或可直接投產的操作程序。算例全部是教學假設；真正驗收須使用適用版本、合格設備與實測參數。代表照片、示意圖與影片不宣稱為每步製造實拍。","scopeEn":"Conceptual design and data interpretation from public principles, not a vendor recipe or production-ready procedure. All worked inputs are educational assumptions. Real acceptance requires the applicable revision, qualified equipment and measured parameters. Representative media are not claimed as footage of every operation.","workedExample":{"title":"可重算的教學算例","titleEn":"Reproducible teaching example","text":"假設輸入 0.1 mW、SOA 小訊號增益 15 dB、後段損失 3 dB，線性估計輸出=0.1×10^(12/10)=1.585 mW；若已達飽和，此估計須下修。","textEn":"Assume 0.1 mW input, 15 dB small-signal gain and 3 dB downstream loss. Linear output is 0.1×10^(12/10)=1.585 mW; saturation invalidates this extrapolation.","assumptions":"未納入增益飽和、偏振及溫度變化；總光功率不等於訊號功率。","assumptionsEn":"Saturation, polarization and temperature changes are excluded; total optical power is not signal power.","sourceScope":"自行編寫的假想算例；原始資料支援領域原理，不提供這組假設數值。","sourceScopeEn":"Independently authored hypothetical exercise; primary sources support the field, not these chosen inputs."},"diagram":{"type":"photonics","labels":["增益與邊界","整合與反射","雜訊與動態","熱與驗收"],"labelsEn":["Gain and boundaries","Integration and reflection","Noise and dynamics","Heat and acceptance"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"stages":[{"id":"a173-stage01","order":1,"title":"增益與邊界","titleEn":"Gain and boundaries","description":"以三個技術單元完成「增益與邊界」的模型與驗證，六項作業各自留存交付物。","descriptionEn":"Three technical units address Gain and boundaries through six separately saved modeling and verification work packages.","steps":[{"id":"a173-v9-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9c-soaexperiment","v9c-mprint"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"title":"放大器與雷射：模型與設計","titleEn":"Amplifier versus laser: model and design","objective":"以「放大器與雷射」建立可檢驗的物理模型，交付可重算且列明邊界的工程紀錄。","objectiveEn":"Build a falsifiable physical model for amplifier versus laser, with reproducible calculations and stated boundaries.","instruction":"先以師傅示意確認「放大器與雷射」的輸入、輸出與座標，再在學徒工作台完成對應元件或資料流的排列。SOA 以受激放大處理輸入訊號；不希望介面反射形成非預期雷射腔。 用本單元的變數畫出至少兩種設計狀態，說明它們在「比較有無輸入光時的光譜，區分寬頻 ASE 與窄頻自激峰。」的驗證中應有何差異；把待量測參數另列，不以動畫位置當成實際公差。","instructionEn":"Use the mentor view to identify the inputs, outputs and coordinates for amplifier versus laser, then arrange the corresponding components or data flow in the apprentice workspace. An SOA amplifies input signals by stimulated emission; interface reflections should not create an unintended laser cavity. Draw at least two design states using this unit's variables and predict how the following verification distinguishes them: Compare spectra with and without input to separate broad ASE from narrow self-oscillation peaks. List unmeasured parameters separately; animation positions are not manufacturing tolerances.","observation":"比較有無輸入光時的光譜，區分寬頻 ASE 與窄頻自激峰。","observationEn":"Compare spectra with and without input to separate broad ASE from narrow self-oscillation peaks.","failure":"須排除的錯誤假說：補回功率就能完全補回 OSNR。 若觀察不支持預測，先核對基準與單位，再依本步判別量測定位原因；不能只調參到曲線相合。","failureEn":"Incorrect hypothesis to reject: Restoring power fully restores OSNR. If observations disagree, first check references and units, then use this step's discriminating measurement; do not simply tune parameters until curves agree.","check":"提交放大器與雷射的兩狀態模型、變數表，以及能由「比較有無輸入光時的光譜，區分寬頻 ASE 與窄頻自激峰。」反駁模型的預測。","checkEn":"Submit two model states and a variable table for amplifier versus laser, plus a falsifiable prediction using: Compare spectra with and without input to separate broad ASE from narrow self-oscillation peaks.","knowledge":[{"id":"a173-v9-01-k1","title":"本單元物理機制","titleEn":"Unit mechanism","text":"SOA 以受激放大處理輸入訊號；不希望介面反射形成非預期雷射腔。","textEn":"An SOA amplifies input signals by stimulated emission; interface reflections should not create an unintended laser cavity.","sourceIds":["v9c-soaexperiment","v9c-mprint"]},{"id":"a173-v9-01-k2","title":"獨立驗證與證據","titleEn":"Independent verification and evidence","text":"比較有無輸入光時的光譜，區分寬頻 ASE 與窄頻自激峰。","textEn":"Compare spectra with and without input to separate broad ASE from narrow self-oscillation peaks.","sourceIds":["v9c-soaexperiment","v9c-mprint"]},{"id":"a173-v9-01-k3","title":"量化模型與適用邊界","titleEn":"Quantitative model and validity boundary","text":"GdB=10log10(Psignal,out/Psignal,in)，需扣除 ASE 並固定參考面。 未納入增益飽和、偏振及溫度變化；總光功率不等於訊號功率。","textEn":"GdB=10log10(Psignal,out/Psignal,in), with ASE removed and reference planes fixed. Saturation, polarization and temperature changes are excluded; total optical power is not signal power.","sourceIds":["v9c-soaexperiment","v9c-mprint"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要審查「放大器與雷射」，哪項主張或驗證方法有根據？","questionEn":"Which claim or verification is justified when reviewing amplifier versus laser?","options":["SOA 以受激放大處理輸入訊號；不希望介面反射形成非預期雷射腔。","補回功率就能完全補回 OSNR。","所有輸入功率都保持相同小訊號增益。"],"optionsEn":["An SOA amplifies input signals by stimulated emission; interface reflections should not create an unintended laser cavity.","Restoring power fully restores OSNR.","Small-signal gain holds at every input power."],"answer":0,"explanation":"SOA 以受激放大處理輸入訊號；不希望介面反射形成非預期雷射腔。 比較有無輸入光時的光譜，區分寬頻 ASE 與窄頻自激峰。","explanationEn":"An SOA amplifies input signals by stimulated emission; interface reflections should not create an unintended laser cavity. Compare spectra with and without input to separate broad ASE from narrow self-oscillation peaks."}},{"id":"a173-v9-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9c-soaexperiment","v9c-mprint"],"prerequisiteIds":["a173-v9-01"],"title":"放大器與雷射：量測與判別","titleEn":"Amplifier versus laser: measurement and diagnosis","objective":"以「放大器與雷射」區分機制並作出有證據的驗收決定，交付可重算且列明邊界的工程紀錄。","objectiveEn":"Discriminate mechanisms and make an evidence-based acceptance decision for amplifier versus laser, with reproducible calculations and stated boundaries.","instruction":"保留上一作業的模型，現在檢驗它是否足以解釋觀察。比較有無輸入光時的光譜，區分寬頻 ASE 與窄頻自激峰。 記錄原始量、單位、基準與重複量測差異；以支持及否定各一項證據比較「SOA 以受激放大處理輸入訊號；不希望介面反射形成非預期雷射腔。」與錯誤假說「所有輸入功率都保持相同小訊號增益。」，最後提出放行、重測或修模決定。","instructionEn":"Retain the previous model and test whether it explains the observations. Compare spectra with and without input to separate broad ASE from narrow self-oscillation peaks. Record raw quantities, units, reference conditions and repeatability. Use supporting and falsifying evidence to compare \"An SOA amplifies input signals by stimulated emission; interface reflections should not create an unintended laser cavity.\" against the incorrect hypothesis \"Small-signal gain holds at every input power.\"; decide whether to accept, repeat or revise the model.","observation":"比較有無輸入光時的光譜，區分寬頻 ASE 與窄頻自激峰。","observationEn":"Compare spectra with and without input to separate broad ASE from narrow self-oscillation peaks.","failure":"須排除的錯誤假說：所有輸入功率都保持相同小訊號增益。 若觀察不支持預測，先核對基準與單位，再依本步判別量測定位原因；不能只調參到曲線相合。","failureEn":"Incorrect hypothesis to reject: Small-signal gain holds at every input power. If observations disagree, first check references and units, then use this step's discriminating measurement; do not simply tune parameters until curves agree.","check":"提交放大器與雷射的量測判別表：比較有無輸入光時的光譜，區分寬頻 ASE 與窄頻自激峰。 附上基準、重複性或不確定度，及不能由本資料判定的結論。","checkEn":"Submit a measurement-discrimination table for amplifier versus laser: Compare spectra with and without input to separate broad ASE from narrow self-oscillation peaks. Include the reference, repeatability or uncertainty, and conclusions the data cannot support.","knowledge":[{"id":"a173-v9-02-k1","title":"本單元物理機制","titleEn":"Unit mechanism","text":"SOA 以受激放大處理輸入訊號；不希望介面反射形成非預期雷射腔。","textEn":"An SOA amplifies input signals by stimulated emission; interface reflections should not create an unintended laser cavity.","sourceIds":["v9c-soaexperiment","v9c-mprint"]},{"id":"a173-v9-02-k2","title":"獨立驗證與證據","titleEn":"Independent verification and evidence","text":"比較有無輸入光時的光譜，區分寬頻 ASE 與窄頻自激峰。","textEn":"Compare spectra with and without input to separate broad ASE from narrow self-oscillation peaks.","sourceIds":["v9c-soaexperiment","v9c-mprint"]},{"id":"a173-v9-02-k3","title":"量化模型與適用邊界","titleEn":"Quantitative model and validity boundary","text":"GdB=10log10(Psignal,out/Psignal,in)，需扣除 ASE 並固定參考面。 未納入增益飽和、偏振及溫度變化；總光功率不等於訊號功率。","textEn":"GdB=10log10(Psignal,out/Psignal,in), with ASE removed and reference planes fixed. Saturation, polarization and temperature changes are excluded; total optical power is not signal power.","sourceIds":["v9c-soaexperiment","v9c-mprint"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要審查「放大器與雷射」，哪項主張或驗證方法有根據？","questionEn":"Which claim or verification is justified when reviewing amplifier versus laser?","options":["ASE 全部是有用的調變訊號。","比較有無輸入光時的光譜，區分寬頻 ASE 與窄頻自激峰。","所有輸入功率都保持相同小訊號增益。"],"optionsEn":["All ASE is useful modulated signal.","Compare spectra with and without input to separate broad ASE from narrow self-oscillation peaks.","Small-signal gain holds at every input power."],"answer":1,"explanation":"SOA 以受激放大處理輸入訊號；不希望介面反射形成非預期雷射腔。 比較有無輸入光時的光譜，區分寬頻 ASE 與窄頻自激峰。","explanationEn":"An SOA amplifies input signals by stimulated emission; interface reflections should not create an unintended laser cavity. Compare spectra with and without input to separate broad ASE from narrow self-oscillation peaks."}},{"id":"a173-v9-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9c-soaexperiment","v9c-mprint"],"prerequisiteIds":["a173-v9-02"],"title":"小訊號增益：模型與設計","titleEn":"Small-signal gain: model and design","objective":"以「小訊號增益」建立可檢驗的物理模型，交付可重算且列明邊界的工程紀錄。","objectiveEn":"Build a falsifiable physical model for small-signal gain, with reproducible calculations and stated boundaries.","instruction":"先以師傅示意確認「小訊號增益」的輸入、輸出與座標，再在學徒工作台完成對應元件或資料流的排列。增益應在同一光功率參考面與偏振定義下量測，接合損失不可忽略。 用本單元的變數畫出至少兩種設計狀態，說明它們在「同時報晶片內部增益與端到端增益，保存去嵌入假設。」的驗證中應有何差異；把待量測參數另列，不以動畫位置當成實際公差。","instructionEn":"Use the mentor view to identify the inputs, outputs and coordinates for small-signal gain, then arrange the corresponding components or data flow in the apprentice workspace. Gain needs consistent power planes and polarization; coupling losses cannot be omitted. Draw at least two design states using this unit's variables and predict how the following verification distinguishes them: Report internal and end-to-end gain together, retaining de-embedding assumptions. List unmeasured parameters separately; animation positions are not manufacturing tolerances.","observation":"同時報晶片內部增益與端到端增益，保存去嵌入假設。","observationEn":"Report internal and end-to-end gain together, retaining de-embedding assumptions.","failure":"須排除的錯誤假說：所有輸入功率都保持相同小訊號增益。 若觀察不支持預測，先核對基準與單位，再依本步判別量測定位原因；不能只調參到曲線相合。","failureEn":"Incorrect hypothesis to reject: Small-signal gain holds at every input power. If observations disagree, first check references and units, then use this step's discriminating measurement; do not simply tune parameters until curves agree.","check":"提交小訊號增益的兩狀態模型、變數表，以及能由「同時報晶片內部增益與端到端增益，保存去嵌入假設。」反駁模型的預測。","checkEn":"Submit two model states and a variable table for small-signal gain, plus a falsifiable prediction using: Report internal and end-to-end gain together, retaining de-embedding assumptions.","knowledge":[{"id":"a173-v9-03-k1","title":"本單元物理機制","titleEn":"Unit mechanism","text":"增益應在同一光功率參考面與偏振定義下量測，接合損失不可忽略。","textEn":"Gain needs consistent power planes and polarization; coupling losses cannot be omitted.","sourceIds":["v9c-soaexperiment","v9c-mprint"]},{"id":"a173-v9-03-k2","title":"獨立驗證與證據","titleEn":"Independent verification and evidence","text":"同時報晶片內部增益與端到端增益，保存去嵌入假設。","textEn":"Report internal and end-to-end gain together, retaining de-embedding assumptions.","sourceIds":["v9c-soaexperiment","v9c-mprint"]},{"id":"a173-v9-03-k3","title":"量化模型與適用邊界","titleEn":"Quantitative model and validity boundary","text":"GdB=10log10(Psignal,out/Psignal,in)，需扣除 ASE 並固定參考面。 未納入增益飽和、偏振及溫度變化；總光功率不等於訊號功率。","textEn":"GdB=10log10(Psignal,out/Psignal,in), with ASE removed and reference planes fixed. Saturation, polarization and temperature changes are excluded; total optical power is not signal power.","sourceIds":["v9c-soaexperiment","v9c-mprint"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要審查「小訊號增益」，哪項主張或驗證方法有根據？","questionEn":"Which claim or verification is justified when reviewing small-signal gain?","options":["所有輸入功率都保持相同小訊號增益。","ASE 全部是有用的調變訊號。","增益應在同一光功率參考面與偏振定義下量測，接合損失不可忽略。"],"optionsEn":["Small-signal gain holds at every input power.","All ASE is useful modulated signal.","Gain needs consistent power planes and polarization; coupling losses cannot be omitted."],"answer":2,"explanation":"增益應在同一光功率參考面與偏振定義下量測，接合損失不可忽略。 同時報晶片內部增益與端到端增益，保存去嵌入假設。","explanationEn":"Gain needs consistent power planes and polarization; coupling losses cannot be omitted. Report internal and end-to-end gain together, retaining de-embedding assumptions."}},{"id":"a173-v9-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9c-soaexperiment","v9c-mprint"],"prerequisiteIds":["a173-v9-03"],"title":"小訊號增益：量測與判別","titleEn":"Small-signal gain: measurement and diagnosis","objective":"以「小訊號增益」區分機制並作出有證據的驗收決定，交付可重算且列明邊界的工程紀錄。","objectiveEn":"Discriminate mechanisms and make an evidence-based acceptance decision for small-signal gain, with reproducible calculations and stated boundaries.","instruction":"保留上一作業的模型，現在檢驗它是否足以解釋觀察。同時報晶片內部增益與端到端增益，保存去嵌入假設。 記錄原始量、單位、基準與重複量測差異；以支持及否定各一項證據比較「增益應在同一光功率參考面與偏振定義下量測，接合損失不可忽略。」與錯誤假說「ASE 全部是有用的調變訊號。」，最後提出放行、重測或修模決定。","instructionEn":"Retain the previous model and test whether it explains the observations. Report internal and end-to-end gain together, retaining de-embedding assumptions. Record raw quantities, units, reference conditions and repeatability. Use supporting and falsifying evidence to compare \"Gain needs consistent power planes and polarization; coupling losses cannot be omitted.\" against the incorrect hypothesis \"All ASE is useful modulated signal.\"; decide whether to accept, repeat or revise the model.","observation":"同時報晶片內部增益與端到端增益，保存去嵌入假設。","observationEn":"Report internal and end-to-end gain together, retaining de-embedding assumptions.","failure":"須排除的錯誤假說：ASE 全部是有用的調變訊號。 若觀察不支持預測，先核對基準與單位，再依本步判別量測定位原因；不能只調參到曲線相合。","failureEn":"Incorrect hypothesis to reject: All ASE is useful modulated signal. If observations disagree, first check references and units, then use this step's discriminating measurement; do not simply tune parameters until curves agree.","check":"提交小訊號增益的量測判別表：同時報晶片內部增益與端到端增益，保存去嵌入假設。 附上基準、重複性或不確定度，及不能由本資料判定的結論。","checkEn":"Submit a measurement-discrimination table for small-signal gain: Report internal and end-to-end gain together, retaining de-embedding assumptions. Include the reference, repeatability or uncertainty, and conclusions the data cannot support.","knowledge":[{"id":"a173-v9-04-k1","title":"本單元物理機制","titleEn":"Unit mechanism","text":"增益應在同一光功率參考面與偏振定義下量測，接合損失不可忽略。","textEn":"Gain needs consistent power planes and polarization; coupling losses cannot be omitted.","sourceIds":["v9c-soaexperiment","v9c-mprint"]},{"id":"a173-v9-04-k2","title":"獨立驗證與證據","titleEn":"Independent verification and evidence","text":"同時報晶片內部增益與端到端增益，保存去嵌入假設。","textEn":"Report internal and end-to-end gain together, retaining de-embedding assumptions.","sourceIds":["v9c-soaexperiment","v9c-mprint"]},{"id":"a173-v9-04-k3","title":"量化模型與適用邊界","titleEn":"Quantitative model and validity boundary","text":"GdB=10log10(Psignal,out/Psignal,in)，需扣除 ASE 並固定參考面。 未納入增益飽和、偏振及溫度變化；總光功率不等於訊號功率。","textEn":"GdB=10log10(Psignal,out/Psignal,in), with ASE removed and reference planes fixed. Saturation, polarization and temperature changes are excluded; total optical power is not signal power.","sourceIds":["v9c-soaexperiment","v9c-mprint"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要審查「小訊號增益」，哪項主張或驗證方法有根據？","questionEn":"Which claim or verification is justified when reviewing small-signal gain?","options":["同時報晶片內部增益與端到端增益，保存去嵌入假設。","ASE 全部是有用的調變訊號。","補回功率就能完全補回 OSNR。"],"optionsEn":["Report internal and end-to-end gain together, retaining de-embedding assumptions.","All ASE is useful modulated signal.","Restoring power fully restores OSNR."],"answer":0,"explanation":"增益應在同一光功率參考面與偏振定義下量測，接合損失不可忽略。 同時報晶片內部增益與端到端增益，保存去嵌入假設。","explanationEn":"Gain needs consistent power planes and polarization; coupling losses cannot be omitted. Report internal and end-to-end gain together, retaining de-embedding assumptions."}},{"id":"a173-v9-05","order":5,"sequence":5,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9c-soaexperiment","v9c-mprint"],"prerequisiteIds":["a173-v9-04"],"title":"飽和與輸出：模型與設計","titleEn":"Saturation and output: model and design","objective":"以「飽和與輸出」建立可檢驗的物理模型，交付可重算且列明邊界的工程紀錄。","objectiveEn":"Build a falsifiable physical model for saturation and output, with reproducible calculations and stated boundaries.","instruction":"先以師傅示意確認「飽和與輸出」的輸入、輸出與座標，再在學徒工作台完成對應元件或資料流的排列。輸入增加會耗盡可用載子，使增益壓縮；固定增益只適用弱訊號。 用本單元的變數畫出至少兩種設計狀態，說明它們在「按算例畫線性外推，再用假想飽和曲線找出偏離區。」的驗證中應有何差異；把待量測參數另列，不以動畫位置當成實際公差。 假設輸入 0.1 mW、SOA 小訊號增益 15 dB、後段損失 3 dB，線性估計輸出=0.1×10^(12/10)=1.585 mW；若已達飽和，此估計須下修。","instructionEn":"Use the mentor view to identify the inputs, outputs and coordinates for saturation and output, then arrange the corresponding components or data flow in the apprentice workspace. Increasing input depletes carriers and compresses gain; constant gain applies only to weak signals. Draw at least two design states using this unit's variables and predict how the following verification distinguishes them: Plot the example's linear extrapolation, then locate deviation using a hypothetical saturation curve. List unmeasured parameters separately; animation positions are not manufacturing tolerances. Assume 0.1 mW input, 15 dB small-signal gain and 3 dB downstream loss. Linear output is 0.1×10^(12/10)=1.585 mW; saturation invalidates this extrapolation.","observation":"按算例畫線性外推，再用假想飽和曲線找出偏離區。","observationEn":"Plot the example's linear extrapolation, then locate deviation using a hypothetical saturation curve.","failure":"須排除的錯誤假說：ASE 全部是有用的調變訊號。 若觀察不支持預測，先核對基準與單位，再依本步判別量測定位原因；不能只調參到曲線相合。","failureEn":"Incorrect hypothesis to reject: All ASE is useful modulated signal. If observations disagree, first check references and units, then use this step's discriminating measurement; do not simply tune parameters until curves agree.","check":"提交飽和與輸出的兩狀態模型、變數表，以及能由「按算例畫線性外推，再用假想飽和曲線找出偏離區。」反駁模型的預測。","checkEn":"Submit two model states and a variable table for saturation and output, plus a falsifiable prediction using: Plot the example's linear extrapolation, then locate deviation using a hypothetical saturation curve.","knowledge":[{"id":"a173-v9-05-k1","title":"本單元物理機制","titleEn":"Unit mechanism","text":"輸入增加會耗盡可用載子，使增益壓縮；固定增益只適用弱訊號。","textEn":"Increasing input depletes carriers and compresses gain; constant gain applies only to weak signals.","sourceIds":["v9c-soaexperiment","v9c-mprint"]},{"id":"a173-v9-05-k2","title":"獨立驗證與證據","titleEn":"Independent verification and evidence","text":"按算例畫線性外推，再用假想飽和曲線找出偏離區。","textEn":"Plot the example's linear extrapolation, then locate deviation using a hypothetical saturation curve.","sourceIds":["v9c-soaexperiment","v9c-mprint"]},{"id":"a173-v9-05-k3","title":"量化模型與適用邊界","titleEn":"Quantitative model and validity boundary","text":"GdB=10log10(Psignal,out/Psignal,in)，需扣除 ASE 並固定參考面。 未納入增益飽和、偏振及溫度變化；總光功率不等於訊號功率。","textEn":"GdB=10log10(Psignal,out/Psignal,in), with ASE removed and reference planes fixed. Saturation, polarization and temperature changes are excluded; total optical power is not signal power.","sourceIds":["v9c-soaexperiment","v9c-mprint"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要審查「飽和與輸出」，哪項主張或驗證方法有根據？","questionEn":"Which claim or verification is justified when reviewing saturation and output?","options":["補回功率就能完全補回 OSNR。","輸入增加會耗盡可用載子，使增益壓縮；固定增益只適用弱訊號。","ASE 全部是有用的調變訊號。"],"optionsEn":["Restoring power fully restores OSNR.","Increasing input depletes carriers and compresses gain; constant gain applies only to weak signals.","All ASE is useful modulated signal."],"answer":1,"explanation":"輸入增加會耗盡可用載子，使增益壓縮；固定增益只適用弱訊號。 按算例畫線性外推，再用假想飽和曲線找出偏離區。","explanationEn":"Increasing input depletes carriers and compresses gain; constant gain applies only to weak signals. Plot the example's linear extrapolation, then locate deviation using a hypothetical saturation curve."}},{"id":"a173-v9-06","order":6,"sequence":6,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9c-soaexperiment","v9c-mprint"],"prerequisiteIds":["a173-v9-05"],"title":"飽和與輸出：量測與判別","titleEn":"Saturation and output: measurement and diagnosis","objective":"以「飽和與輸出」區分機制並作出有證據的驗收決定，交付可重算且列明邊界的工程紀錄。","objectiveEn":"Discriminate mechanisms and make an evidence-based acceptance decision for saturation and output, with reproducible calculations and stated boundaries.","instruction":"保留上一作業的模型，現在檢驗它是否足以解釋觀察。按算例畫線性外推，再用假想飽和曲線找出偏離區。 記錄原始量、單位、基準與重複量測差異；以支持及否定各一項證據比較「輸入增加會耗盡可用載子，使增益壓縮；固定增益只適用弱訊號。」與錯誤假說「補回功率就能完全補回 OSNR。」，最後提出放行、重測或修模決定。 假設輸入 0.1 mW、SOA 小訊號增益 15 dB、後段損失 3 dB，線性估計輸出=0.1×10^(12/10)=1.585 mW；若已達飽和，此估計須下修。","instructionEn":"Retain the previous model and test whether it explains the observations. Plot the example's linear extrapolation, then locate deviation using a hypothetical saturation curve. Record raw quantities, units, reference conditions and repeatability. Use supporting and falsifying evidence to compare \"Increasing input depletes carriers and compresses gain; constant gain applies only to weak signals.\" against the incorrect hypothesis \"Restoring power fully restores OSNR.\"; decide whether to accept, repeat or revise the model. Assume 0.1 mW input, 15 dB small-signal gain and 3 dB downstream loss. Linear output is 0.1×10^(12/10)=1.585 mW; saturation invalidates this extrapolation.","observation":"按算例畫線性外推，再用假想飽和曲線找出偏離區。","observationEn":"Plot the example's linear extrapolation, then locate deviation using a hypothetical saturation curve.","failure":"須排除的錯誤假說：補回功率就能完全補回 OSNR。 若觀察不支持預測，先核對基準與單位，再依本步判別量測定位原因；不能只調參到曲線相合。","failureEn":"Incorrect hypothesis to reject: Restoring power fully restores OSNR. If observations disagree, first check references and units, then use this step's discriminating measurement; do not simply tune parameters until curves agree.","check":"提交飽和與輸出的量測判別表：按算例畫線性外推，再用假想飽和曲線找出偏離區。 附上基準、重複性或不確定度，及不能由本資料判定的結論。","checkEn":"Submit a measurement-discrimination table for saturation and output: Plot the example's linear extrapolation, then locate deviation using a hypothetical saturation curve. Include the reference, repeatability or uncertainty, and conclusions the data cannot support.","knowledge":[{"id":"a173-v9-06-k1","title":"本單元物理機制","titleEn":"Unit mechanism","text":"輸入增加會耗盡可用載子，使增益壓縮；固定增益只適用弱訊號。","textEn":"Increasing input depletes carriers and compresses gain; constant gain applies only to weak signals.","sourceIds":["v9c-soaexperiment","v9c-mprint"]},{"id":"a173-v9-06-k2","title":"獨立驗證與證據","titleEn":"Independent verification and evidence","text":"按算例畫線性外推，再用假想飽和曲線找出偏離區。","textEn":"Plot the example's linear extrapolation, then locate deviation using a hypothetical saturation curve.","sourceIds":["v9c-soaexperiment","v9c-mprint"]},{"id":"a173-v9-06-k3","title":"量化模型與適用邊界","titleEn":"Quantitative model and validity boundary","text":"GdB=10log10(Psignal,out/Psignal,in)，需扣除 ASE 並固定參考面。 未納入增益飽和、偏振及溫度變化；總光功率不等於訊號功率。","textEn":"GdB=10log10(Psignal,out/Psignal,in), with ASE removed and reference planes fixed. Saturation, polarization and temperature changes are excluded; total optical power is not signal power.","sourceIds":["v9c-soaexperiment","v9c-mprint"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要審查「飽和與輸出」，哪項主張或驗證方法有根據？","questionEn":"Which claim or verification is justified when reviewing saturation and output?","options":["補回功率就能完全補回 OSNR。","所有輸入功率都保持相同小訊號增益。","按算例畫線性外推，再用假想飽和曲線找出偏離區。"],"optionsEn":["Restoring power fully restores OSNR.","Small-signal gain holds at every input power.","Plot the example's linear extrapolation, then locate deviation using a hypothetical saturation curve."],"answer":2,"explanation":"輸入增加會耗盡可用載子，使增益壓縮；固定增益只適用弱訊號。 按算例畫線性外推，再用假想飽和曲線找出偏離區。","explanationEn":"Increasing input depletes carriers and compresses gain; constant gain applies only to weak signals. Plot the example's linear extrapolation, then locate deviation using a hypothetical saturation curve."}}]},{"id":"a173-stage02","order":2,"title":"整合與反射","titleEn":"Integration and reflection","description":"以三個技術單元完成「整合與反射」的模型與驗證，六項作業各自留存交付物。","descriptionEn":"Three technical units address Integration and reflection through six separately saved modeling and verification work packages.","steps":[{"id":"a173-v9-07","order":1,"sequence":7,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9c-soaexperiment","v9c-mprint"],"prerequisiteIds":["a173-v9-06"],"title":"倏逝轉接：模型與設計","titleEn":"Evanescent transition: model and design","objective":"以「倏逝轉接」建立可檢驗的物理模型，交付可重算且列明邊界的工程紀錄。","objectiveEn":"Build a falsifiable physical model for evanescent transition, with reproducible calculations and stated boundaries.","instruction":"先以師傅示意確認「倏逝轉接」的輸入、輸出與座標，再在學徒工作台完成對應元件或資料流的排列。III-V 到矽的轉換器控制模態重疊與反射，不能只看末端對準。 用本單元的變數畫出至少兩種設計狀態，說明它們在「比較波長掃描與反射曲線，找出漸變不足或間隙偏移。」的驗證中應有何差異；把待量測參數另列，不以動畫位置當成實際公差。","instructionEn":"Use the mentor view to identify the inputs, outputs and coordinates for evanescent transition, then arrange the corresponding components or data flow in the apprentice workspace. The III-V-to-silicon transition controls modal overlap and reflection, not just endpoint alignment. Draw at least two design states using this unit's variables and predict how the following verification distinguishes them: Compare wavelength sweeps and reflection curves for insufficient tapering or gap shifts. List unmeasured parameters separately; animation positions are not manufacturing tolerances.","observation":"比較波長掃描與反射曲線，找出漸變不足或間隙偏移。","observationEn":"Compare wavelength sweeps and reflection curves for insufficient tapering or gap shifts.","failure":"須排除的錯誤假說：補回功率就能完全補回 OSNR。 若觀察不支持預測，先核對基準與單位，再依本步判別量測定位原因；不能只調參到曲線相合。","failureEn":"Incorrect hypothesis to reject: Restoring power fully restores OSNR. If observations disagree, first check references and units, then use this step's discriminating measurement; do not simply tune parameters until curves agree.","check":"提交倏逝轉接的兩狀態模型、變數表，以及能由「比較波長掃描與反射曲線，找出漸變不足或間隙偏移。」反駁模型的預測。","checkEn":"Submit two model states and a variable table for evanescent transition, plus a falsifiable prediction using: Compare wavelength sweeps and reflection curves for insufficient tapering or gap shifts.","knowledge":[{"id":"a173-v9-07-k1","title":"本單元物理機制","titleEn":"Unit mechanism","text":"III-V 到矽的轉換器控制模態重疊與反射，不能只看末端對準。","textEn":"The III-V-to-silicon transition controls modal overlap and reflection, not just endpoint alignment.","sourceIds":["v9c-soaexperiment","v9c-mprint"]},{"id":"a173-v9-07-k2","title":"獨立驗證與證據","titleEn":"Independent verification and evidence","text":"比較波長掃描與反射曲線，找出漸變不足或間隙偏移。","textEn":"Compare wavelength sweeps and reflection curves for insufficient tapering or gap shifts.","sourceIds":["v9c-soaexperiment","v9c-mprint"]},{"id":"a173-v9-07-k3","title":"量化模型與適用邊界","titleEn":"Quantitative model and validity boundary","text":"GdB=10log10(Psignal,out/Psignal,in)，需扣除 ASE 並固定參考面。 未納入增益飽和、偏振及溫度變化；總光功率不等於訊號功率。","textEn":"GdB=10log10(Psignal,out/Psignal,in), with ASE removed and reference planes fixed. Saturation, polarization and temperature changes are excluded; total optical power is not signal power.","sourceIds":["v9c-soaexperiment","v9c-mprint"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要審查「倏逝轉接」，哪項主張或驗證方法有根據？","questionEn":"Which claim or verification is justified when reviewing evanescent transition?","options":["III-V 到矽的轉換器控制模態重疊與反射，不能只看末端對準。","補回功率就能完全補回 OSNR。","所有輸入功率都保持相同小訊號增益。"],"optionsEn":["The III-V-to-silicon transition controls modal overlap and reflection, not just endpoint alignment.","Restoring power fully restores OSNR.","Small-signal gain holds at every input power."],"answer":0,"explanation":"III-V 到矽的轉換器控制模態重疊與反射，不能只看末端對準。 比較波長掃描與反射曲線，找出漸變不足或間隙偏移。","explanationEn":"The III-V-to-silicon transition controls modal overlap and reflection, not just endpoint alignment. Compare wavelength sweeps and reflection curves for insufficient tapering or gap shifts."}},{"id":"a173-v9-08","order":2,"sequence":8,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9c-soaexperiment","v9c-mprint"],"prerequisiteIds":["a173-v9-07"],"title":"倏逝轉接：量測與判別","titleEn":"Evanescent transition: measurement and diagnosis","objective":"以「倏逝轉接」區分機制並作出有證據的驗收決定，交付可重算且列明邊界的工程紀錄。","objectiveEn":"Discriminate mechanisms and make an evidence-based acceptance decision for evanescent transition, with reproducible calculations and stated boundaries.","instruction":"保留上一作業的模型，現在檢驗它是否足以解釋觀察。比較波長掃描與反射曲線，找出漸變不足或間隙偏移。 記錄原始量、單位、基準與重複量測差異；以支持及否定各一項證據比較「III-V 到矽的轉換器控制模態重疊與反射，不能只看末端對準。」與錯誤假說「所有輸入功率都保持相同小訊號增益。」，最後提出放行、重測或修模決定。","instructionEn":"Retain the previous model and test whether it explains the observations. Compare wavelength sweeps and reflection curves for insufficient tapering or gap shifts. Record raw quantities, units, reference conditions and repeatability. Use supporting and falsifying evidence to compare \"The III-V-to-silicon transition controls modal overlap and reflection, not just endpoint alignment.\" against the incorrect hypothesis \"Small-signal gain holds at every input power.\"; decide whether to accept, repeat or revise the model.","observation":"比較波長掃描與反射曲線，找出漸變不足或間隙偏移。","observationEn":"Compare wavelength sweeps and reflection curves for insufficient tapering or gap shifts.","failure":"須排除的錯誤假說：所有輸入功率都保持相同小訊號增益。 若觀察不支持預測，先核對基準與單位，再依本步判別量測定位原因；不能只調參到曲線相合。","failureEn":"Incorrect hypothesis to reject: Small-signal gain holds at every input power. If observations disagree, first check references and units, then use this step's discriminating measurement; do not simply tune parameters until curves agree.","check":"提交倏逝轉接的量測判別表：比較波長掃描與反射曲線，找出漸變不足或間隙偏移。 附上基準、重複性或不確定度，及不能由本資料判定的結論。","checkEn":"Submit a measurement-discrimination table for evanescent transition: Compare wavelength sweeps and reflection curves for insufficient tapering or gap shifts. Include the reference, repeatability or uncertainty, and conclusions the data cannot support.","knowledge":[{"id":"a173-v9-08-k1","title":"本單元物理機制","titleEn":"Unit mechanism","text":"III-V 到矽的轉換器控制模態重疊與反射，不能只看末端對準。","textEn":"The III-V-to-silicon transition controls modal overlap and reflection, not just endpoint alignment.","sourceIds":["v9c-soaexperiment","v9c-mprint"]},{"id":"a173-v9-08-k2","title":"獨立驗證與證據","titleEn":"Independent verification and evidence","text":"比較波長掃描與反射曲線，找出漸變不足或間隙偏移。","textEn":"Compare wavelength sweeps and reflection curves for insufficient tapering or gap shifts.","sourceIds":["v9c-soaexperiment","v9c-mprint"]},{"id":"a173-v9-08-k3","title":"量化模型與適用邊界","titleEn":"Quantitative model and validity boundary","text":"GdB=10log10(Psignal,out/Psignal,in)，需扣除 ASE 並固定參考面。 未納入增益飽和、偏振及溫度變化；總光功率不等於訊號功率。","textEn":"GdB=10log10(Psignal,out/Psignal,in), with ASE removed and reference planes fixed. Saturation, polarization and temperature changes are excluded; total optical power is not signal power.","sourceIds":["v9c-soaexperiment","v9c-mprint"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要審查「倏逝轉接」，哪項主張或驗證方法有根據？","questionEn":"Which claim or verification is justified when reviewing evanescent transition?","options":["ASE 全部是有用的調變訊號。","比較波長掃描與反射曲線，找出漸變不足或間隙偏移。","所有輸入功率都保持相同小訊號增益。"],"optionsEn":["All ASE is useful modulated signal.","Compare wavelength sweeps and reflection curves for insufficient tapering or gap shifts.","Small-signal gain holds at every input power."],"answer":1,"explanation":"III-V 到矽的轉換器控制模態重疊與反射，不能只看末端對準。 比較波長掃描與反射曲線，找出漸變不足或間隙偏移。","explanationEn":"The III-V-to-silicon transition controls modal overlap and reflection, not just endpoint alignment. Compare wavelength sweeps and reflection curves for insufficient tapering or gap shifts."}},{"id":"a173-v9-09","order":3,"sequence":9,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9c-soaexperiment","v9c-mprint"],"prerequisiteIds":["a173-v9-08"],"title":"端面反射：模型與設計","titleEn":"Facet reflection: model and design","objective":"以「端面反射」建立可檢驗的物理模型，交付可重算且列明邊界的工程紀錄。","objectiveEn":"Build a falsifiable physical model for facet reflection, with reproducible calculations and stated boundaries.","instruction":"先以師傅示意確認「端面反射」的輸入、輸出與座標，再在學徒工作台完成對應元件或資料流的排列。往返增益若克服總損耗可能自激；單程增益合格不代表回路穩定。 用本單元的變數畫出至少兩種設計狀態，說明它們在「畫最短反射回路並列每次通過的增益與損耗。」的驗證中應有何差異；把待量測參數另列，不以動畫位置當成實際公差。","instructionEn":"Use the mentor view to identify the inputs, outputs and coordinates for facet reflection, then arrange the corresponding components or data flow in the apprentice workspace. Round-trip gain exceeding loss can self-oscillate; acceptable single-pass gain does not ensure loop stability. Draw at least two design states using this unit's variables and predict how the following verification distinguishes them: Draw the shortest reflection loop and list gain and loss for every pass. List unmeasured parameters separately; animation positions are not manufacturing tolerances.","observation":"畫最短反射回路並列每次通過的增益與損耗。","observationEn":"Draw the shortest reflection loop and list gain and loss for every pass.","failure":"須排除的錯誤假說：所有輸入功率都保持相同小訊號增益。 若觀察不支持預測，先核對基準與單位，再依本步判別量測定位原因；不能只調參到曲線相合。","failureEn":"Incorrect hypothesis to reject: Small-signal gain holds at every input power. If observations disagree, first check references and units, then use this step's discriminating measurement; do not simply tune parameters until curves agree.","check":"提交端面反射的兩狀態模型、變數表，以及能由「畫最短反射回路並列每次通過的增益與損耗。」反駁模型的預測。","checkEn":"Submit two model states and a variable table for facet reflection, plus a falsifiable prediction using: Draw the shortest reflection loop and list gain and loss for every pass.","knowledge":[{"id":"a173-v9-09-k1","title":"本單元物理機制","titleEn":"Unit mechanism","text":"往返增益若克服總損耗可能自激；單程增益合格不代表回路穩定。","textEn":"Round-trip gain exceeding loss can self-oscillate; acceptable single-pass gain does not ensure loop stability.","sourceIds":["v9c-soaexperiment","v9c-mprint"]},{"id":"a173-v9-09-k2","title":"獨立驗證與證據","titleEn":"Independent verification and evidence","text":"畫最短反射回路並列每次通過的增益與損耗。","textEn":"Draw the shortest reflection loop and list gain and loss for every pass.","sourceIds":["v9c-soaexperiment","v9c-mprint"]},{"id":"a173-v9-09-k3","title":"量化模型與適用邊界","titleEn":"Quantitative model and validity boundary","text":"GdB=10log10(Psignal,out/Psignal,in)，需扣除 ASE 並固定參考面。 未納入增益飽和、偏振及溫度變化；總光功率不等於訊號功率。","textEn":"GdB=10log10(Psignal,out/Psignal,in), with ASE removed and reference planes fixed. Saturation, polarization and temperature changes are excluded; total optical power is not signal power.","sourceIds":["v9c-soaexperiment","v9c-mprint"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要審查「端面反射」，哪項主張或驗證方法有根據？","questionEn":"Which claim or verification is justified when reviewing facet reflection?","options":["所有輸入功率都保持相同小訊號增益。","ASE 全部是有用的調變訊號。","往返增益若克服總損耗可能自激；單程增益合格不代表回路穩定。"],"optionsEn":["Small-signal gain holds at every input power.","All ASE is useful modulated signal.","Round-trip gain exceeding loss can self-oscillate; acceptable single-pass gain does not ensure loop stability."],"answer":2,"explanation":"往返增益若克服總損耗可能自激；單程增益合格不代表回路穩定。 畫最短反射回路並列每次通過的增益與損耗。","explanationEn":"Round-trip gain exceeding loss can self-oscillate; acceptable single-pass gain does not ensure loop stability. Draw the shortest reflection loop and list gain and loss for every pass."}},{"id":"a173-v9-10","order":4,"sequence":10,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9c-soaexperiment","v9c-mprint"],"prerequisiteIds":["a173-v9-09"],"title":"端面反射：量測與判別","titleEn":"Facet reflection: measurement and diagnosis","objective":"以「端面反射」區分機制並作出有證據的驗收決定，交付可重算且列明邊界的工程紀錄。","objectiveEn":"Discriminate mechanisms and make an evidence-based acceptance decision for facet reflection, with reproducible calculations and stated boundaries.","instruction":"保留上一作業的模型，現在檢驗它是否足以解釋觀察。畫最短反射回路並列每次通過的增益與損耗。 記錄原始量、單位、基準與重複量測差異；以支持及否定各一項證據比較「往返增益若克服總損耗可能自激；單程增益合格不代表回路穩定。」與錯誤假說「ASE 全部是有用的調變訊號。」，最後提出放行、重測或修模決定。","instructionEn":"Retain the previous model and test whether it explains the observations. Draw the shortest reflection loop and list gain and loss for every pass. Record raw quantities, units, reference conditions and repeatability. Use supporting and falsifying evidence to compare \"Round-trip gain exceeding loss can self-oscillate; acceptable single-pass gain does not ensure loop stability.\" against the incorrect hypothesis \"All ASE is useful modulated signal.\"; decide whether to accept, repeat or revise the model.","observation":"畫最短反射回路並列每次通過的增益與損耗。","observationEn":"Draw the shortest reflection loop and list gain and loss for every pass.","failure":"須排除的錯誤假說：ASE 全部是有用的調變訊號。 若觀察不支持預測，先核對基準與單位，再依本步判別量測定位原因；不能只調參到曲線相合。","failureEn":"Incorrect hypothesis to reject: All ASE is useful modulated signal. If observations disagree, first check references and units, then use this step's discriminating measurement; do not simply tune parameters until curves agree.","check":"提交端面反射的量測判別表：畫最短反射回路並列每次通過的增益與損耗。 附上基準、重複性或不確定度，及不能由本資料判定的結論。","checkEn":"Submit a measurement-discrimination table for facet reflection: Draw the shortest reflection loop and list gain and loss for every pass. Include the reference, repeatability or uncertainty, and conclusions the data cannot support.","knowledge":[{"id":"a173-v9-10-k1","title":"本單元物理機制","titleEn":"Unit mechanism","text":"往返增益若克服總損耗可能自激；單程增益合格不代表回路穩定。","textEn":"Round-trip gain exceeding loss can self-oscillate; acceptable single-pass gain does not ensure loop stability.","sourceIds":["v9c-soaexperiment","v9c-mprint"]},{"id":"a173-v9-10-k2","title":"獨立驗證與證據","titleEn":"Independent verification and evidence","text":"畫最短反射回路並列每次通過的增益與損耗。","textEn":"Draw the shortest reflection loop and list gain and loss for every pass.","sourceIds":["v9c-soaexperiment","v9c-mprint"]},{"id":"a173-v9-10-k3","title":"量化模型與適用邊界","titleEn":"Quantitative model and validity boundary","text":"GdB=10log10(Psignal,out/Psignal,in)，需扣除 ASE 並固定參考面。 未納入增益飽和、偏振及溫度變化；總光功率不等於訊號功率。","textEn":"GdB=10log10(Psignal,out/Psignal,in), with ASE removed and reference planes fixed. Saturation, polarization and temperature changes are excluded; total optical power is not signal power.","sourceIds":["v9c-soaexperiment","v9c-mprint"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要審查「端面反射」，哪項主張或驗證方法有根據？","questionEn":"Which claim or verification is justified when reviewing facet reflection?","options":["畫最短反射回路並列每次通過的增益與損耗。","ASE 全部是有用的調變訊號。","補回功率就能完全補回 OSNR。"],"optionsEn":["Draw the shortest reflection loop and list gain and loss for every pass.","All ASE is useful modulated signal.","Restoring power fully restores OSNR."],"answer":0,"explanation":"往返增益若克服總損耗可能自激；單程增益合格不代表回路穩定。 畫最短反射回路並列每次通過的增益與損耗。","explanationEn":"Round-trip gain exceeding loss can self-oscillate; acceptable single-pass gain does not ensure loop stability. Draw the shortest reflection loop and list gain and loss for every pass."}},{"id":"a173-v9-11","order":5,"sequence":11,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9c-soaexperiment","v9c-mprint"],"prerequisiteIds":["a173-v9-10"],"title":"偏振相依增益：模型與設計","titleEn":"Polarization-dependent gain: model and design","objective":"以「偏振相依增益」建立可檢驗的物理模型，交付可重算且列明邊界的工程紀錄。","objectiveEn":"Build a falsifiable physical model for polarization-dependent gain, with reproducible calculations and stated boundaries.","instruction":"先以師傅示意確認「偏振相依增益」的輸入、輸出與座標，再在學徒工作台完成對應元件或資料流的排列。TE 與 TM 的受限增益可能不同，偏振漂移可表現為功率波動。 用本單元的變數畫出至少兩種設計狀態，說明它們在「固定總輸入功率掃偏振，將增益變化與溫度漂移分開。」的驗證中應有何差異；把待量測參數另列，不以動畫位置當成實際公差。","instructionEn":"Use the mentor view to identify the inputs, outputs and coordinates for polarization-dependent gain, then arrange the corresponding components or data flow in the apprentice workspace. TE and TM confinement gain can differ; polarization drift can appear as power fluctuation. Draw at least two design states using this unit's variables and predict how the following verification distinguishes them: Sweep polarization at fixed input power and separate gain variation from thermal drift. List unmeasured parameters separately; animation positions are not manufacturing tolerances.","observation":"固定總輸入功率掃偏振，將增益變化與溫度漂移分開。","observationEn":"Sweep polarization at fixed input power and separate gain variation from thermal drift.","failure":"須排除的錯誤假說：ASE 全部是有用的調變訊號。 若觀察不支持預測，先核對基準與單位，再依本步判別量測定位原因；不能只調參到曲線相合。","failureEn":"Incorrect hypothesis to reject: All ASE is useful modulated signal. If observations disagree, first check references and units, then use this step's discriminating measurement; do not simply tune parameters until curves agree.","check":"提交偏振相依增益的兩狀態模型、變數表，以及能由「固定總輸入功率掃偏振，將增益變化與溫度漂移分開。」反駁模型的預測。","checkEn":"Submit two model states and a variable table for polarization-dependent gain, plus a falsifiable prediction using: Sweep polarization at fixed input power and separate gain variation from thermal drift.","knowledge":[{"id":"a173-v9-11-k1","title":"本單元物理機制","titleEn":"Unit mechanism","text":"TE 與 TM 的受限增益可能不同，偏振漂移可表現為功率波動。","textEn":"TE and TM confinement gain can differ; polarization drift can appear as power fluctuation.","sourceIds":["v9c-soaexperiment","v9c-mprint"]},{"id":"a173-v9-11-k2","title":"獨立驗證與證據","titleEn":"Independent verification and evidence","text":"固定總輸入功率掃偏振，將增益變化與溫度漂移分開。","textEn":"Sweep polarization at fixed input power and separate gain variation from thermal drift.","sourceIds":["v9c-soaexperiment","v9c-mprint"]},{"id":"a173-v9-11-k3","title":"量化模型與適用邊界","titleEn":"Quantitative model and validity boundary","text":"GdB=10log10(Psignal,out/Psignal,in)，需扣除 ASE 並固定參考面。 未納入增益飽和、偏振及溫度變化；總光功率不等於訊號功率。","textEn":"GdB=10log10(Psignal,out/Psignal,in), with ASE removed and reference planes fixed. Saturation, polarization and temperature changes are excluded; total optical power is not signal power.","sourceIds":["v9c-soaexperiment","v9c-mprint"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要審查「偏振相依增益」，哪項主張或驗證方法有根據？","questionEn":"Which claim or verification is justified when reviewing polarization-dependent gain?","options":["補回功率就能完全補回 OSNR。","TE 與 TM 的受限增益可能不同，偏振漂移可表現為功率波動。","ASE 全部是有用的調變訊號。"],"optionsEn":["Restoring power fully restores OSNR.","TE and TM confinement gain can differ; polarization drift can appear as power fluctuation.","All ASE is useful modulated signal."],"answer":1,"explanation":"TE 與 TM 的受限增益可能不同，偏振漂移可表現為功率波動。 固定總輸入功率掃偏振，將增益變化與溫度漂移分開。","explanationEn":"TE and TM confinement gain can differ; polarization drift can appear as power fluctuation. Sweep polarization at fixed input power and separate gain variation from thermal drift."}},{"id":"a173-v9-12","order":6,"sequence":12,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9c-soaexperiment","v9c-mprint"],"prerequisiteIds":["a173-v9-11"],"title":"偏振相依增益：量測與判別","titleEn":"Polarization-dependent gain: measurement and diagnosis","objective":"以「偏振相依增益」區分機制並作出有證據的驗收決定，交付可重算且列明邊界的工程紀錄。","objectiveEn":"Discriminate mechanisms and make an evidence-based acceptance decision for polarization-dependent gain, with reproducible calculations and stated boundaries.","instruction":"保留上一作業的模型，現在檢驗它是否足以解釋觀察。固定總輸入功率掃偏振，將增益變化與溫度漂移分開。 記錄原始量、單位、基準與重複量測差異；以支持及否定各一項證據比較「TE 與 TM 的受限增益可能不同，偏振漂移可表現為功率波動。」與錯誤假說「補回功率就能完全補回 OSNR。」，最後提出放行、重測或修模決定。","instructionEn":"Retain the previous model and test whether it explains the observations. Sweep polarization at fixed input power and separate gain variation from thermal drift. Record raw quantities, units, reference conditions and repeatability. Use supporting and falsifying evidence to compare \"TE and TM confinement gain can differ; polarization drift can appear as power fluctuation.\" against the incorrect hypothesis \"Restoring power fully restores OSNR.\"; decide whether to accept, repeat or revise the model.","observation":"固定總輸入功率掃偏振，將增益變化與溫度漂移分開。","observationEn":"Sweep polarization at fixed input power and separate gain variation from thermal drift.","failure":"須排除的錯誤假說：補回功率就能完全補回 OSNR。 若觀察不支持預測，先核對基準與單位，再依本步判別量測定位原因；不能只調參到曲線相合。","failureEn":"Incorrect hypothesis to reject: Restoring power fully restores OSNR. If observations disagree, first check references and units, then use this step's discriminating measurement; do not simply tune parameters until curves agree.","check":"提交偏振相依增益的量測判別表：固定總輸入功率掃偏振，將增益變化與溫度漂移分開。 附上基準、重複性或不確定度，及不能由本資料判定的結論。","checkEn":"Submit a measurement-discrimination table for polarization-dependent gain: Sweep polarization at fixed input power and separate gain variation from thermal drift. Include the reference, repeatability or uncertainty, and conclusions the data cannot support.","knowledge":[{"id":"a173-v9-12-k1","title":"本單元物理機制","titleEn":"Unit mechanism","text":"TE 與 TM 的受限增益可能不同，偏振漂移可表現為功率波動。","textEn":"TE and TM confinement gain can differ; polarization drift can appear as power fluctuation.","sourceIds":["v9c-soaexperiment","v9c-mprint"]},{"id":"a173-v9-12-k2","title":"獨立驗證與證據","titleEn":"Independent verification and evidence","text":"固定總輸入功率掃偏振，將增益變化與溫度漂移分開。","textEn":"Sweep polarization at fixed input power and separate gain variation from thermal drift.","sourceIds":["v9c-soaexperiment","v9c-mprint"]},{"id":"a173-v9-12-k3","title":"量化模型與適用邊界","titleEn":"Quantitative model and validity boundary","text":"GdB=10log10(Psignal,out/Psignal,in)，需扣除 ASE 並固定參考面。 未納入增益飽和、偏振及溫度變化；總光功率不等於訊號功率。","textEn":"GdB=10log10(Psignal,out/Psignal,in), with ASE removed and reference planes fixed. Saturation, polarization and temperature changes are excluded; total optical power is not signal power.","sourceIds":["v9c-soaexperiment","v9c-mprint"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要審查「偏振相依增益」，哪項主張或驗證方法有根據？","questionEn":"Which claim or verification is justified when reviewing polarization-dependent gain?","options":["補回功率就能完全補回 OSNR。","所有輸入功率都保持相同小訊號增益。","固定總輸入功率掃偏振，將增益變化與溫度漂移分開。"],"optionsEn":["Restoring power fully restores OSNR.","Small-signal gain holds at every input power.","Sweep polarization at fixed input power and separate gain variation from thermal drift."],"answer":2,"explanation":"TE 與 TM 的受限增益可能不同，偏振漂移可表現為功率波動。 固定總輸入功率掃偏振，將增益變化與溫度漂移分開。","explanationEn":"TE and TM confinement gain can differ; polarization drift can appear as power fluctuation. Sweep polarization at fixed input power and separate gain variation from thermal drift."}}]},{"id":"a173-stage03","order":3,"title":"雜訊與動態","titleEn":"Noise and dynamics","description":"以三個技術單元完成「雜訊與動態」的模型與驗證，六項作業各自留存交付物。","descriptionEn":"Three technical units address Noise and dynamics through six separately saved modeling and verification work packages.","steps":[{"id":"a173-v9-13","order":1,"sequence":13,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9c-soaexperiment","v9c-mprint"],"prerequisiteIds":["a173-v9-12"],"title":"ASE 頻譜：模型與設計","titleEn":"ASE spectrum: model and design","objective":"以「ASE 頻譜」建立可檢驗的物理模型，交付可重算且列明邊界的工程紀錄。","objectiveEn":"Build a falsifiable physical model for ase spectrum, with reproducible calculations and stated boundaries.","instruction":"先以師傅示意確認「ASE 頻譜」的輸入、輸出與座標，再在學徒工作台完成對應元件或資料流的排列。放大自發輻射增加輸出功率但不等於有用訊號，頻譜積分需要解析頻寬。 用本單元的變數畫出至少兩種設計狀態，說明它們在「量測有無訊號兩種光譜，以相同解析頻寬估计 ASE 底噪。」的驗證中應有何差異；把待量測參數另列，不以動畫位置當成實際公差。","instructionEn":"Use the mentor view to identify the inputs, outputs and coordinates for ase spectrum, then arrange the corresponding components or data flow in the apprentice workspace. Amplified spontaneous emission adds output power but not useful signal; spectral integration requires resolution bandwidth. Draw at least two design states using this unit's variables and predict how the following verification distinguishes them: Measure spectra with and without signal and estimate ASE at identical resolution bandwidth. List unmeasured parameters separately; animation positions are not manufacturing tolerances.","observation":"量測有無訊號兩種光譜，以相同解析頻寬估计 ASE 底噪。","observationEn":"Measure spectra with and without signal and estimate ASE at identical resolution bandwidth.","failure":"須排除的錯誤假說：補回功率就能完全補回 OSNR。 若觀察不支持預測，先核對基準與單位，再依本步判別量測定位原因；不能只調參到曲線相合。","failureEn":"Incorrect hypothesis to reject: Restoring power fully restores OSNR. If observations disagree, first check references and units, then use this step's discriminating measurement; do not simply tune parameters until curves agree.","check":"提交ASE 頻譜的兩狀態模型、變數表，以及能由「量測有無訊號兩種光譜，以相同解析頻寬估计 ASE 底噪。」反駁模型的預測。","checkEn":"Submit two model states and a variable table for ase spectrum, plus a falsifiable prediction using: Measure spectra with and without signal and estimate ASE at identical resolution bandwidth.","knowledge":[{"id":"a173-v9-13-k1","title":"本單元物理機制","titleEn":"Unit mechanism","text":"放大自發輻射增加輸出功率但不等於有用訊號，頻譜積分需要解析頻寬。","textEn":"Amplified spontaneous emission adds output power but not useful signal; spectral integration requires resolution bandwidth.","sourceIds":["v9c-soaexperiment","v9c-mprint"]},{"id":"a173-v9-13-k2","title":"獨立驗證與證據","titleEn":"Independent verification and evidence","text":"量測有無訊號兩種光譜，以相同解析頻寬估计 ASE 底噪。","textEn":"Measure spectra with and without signal and estimate ASE at identical resolution bandwidth.","sourceIds":["v9c-soaexperiment","v9c-mprint"]},{"id":"a173-v9-13-k3","title":"量化模型與適用邊界","titleEn":"Quantitative model and validity boundary","text":"GdB=10log10(Psignal,out/Psignal,in)，需扣除 ASE 並固定參考面。 未納入增益飽和、偏振及溫度變化；總光功率不等於訊號功率。","textEn":"GdB=10log10(Psignal,out/Psignal,in), with ASE removed and reference planes fixed. Saturation, polarization and temperature changes are excluded; total optical power is not signal power.","sourceIds":["v9c-soaexperiment","v9c-mprint"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要審查「ASE 頻譜」，哪項主張或驗證方法有根據？","questionEn":"Which claim or verification is justified when reviewing ase spectrum?","options":["放大自發輻射增加輸出功率但不等於有用訊號，頻譜積分需要解析頻寬。","補回功率就能完全補回 OSNR。","所有輸入功率都保持相同小訊號增益。"],"optionsEn":["Amplified spontaneous emission adds output power but not useful signal; spectral integration requires resolution bandwidth.","Restoring power fully restores OSNR.","Small-signal gain holds at every input power."],"answer":0,"explanation":"放大自發輻射增加輸出功率但不等於有用訊號，頻譜積分需要解析頻寬。 量測有無訊號兩種光譜，以相同解析頻寬估计 ASE 底噪。","explanationEn":"Amplified spontaneous emission adds output power but not useful signal; spectral integration requires resolution bandwidth. Measure spectra with and without signal and estimate ASE at identical resolution bandwidth."}},{"id":"a173-v9-14","order":2,"sequence":14,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9c-soaexperiment","v9c-mprint"],"prerequisiteIds":["a173-v9-13"],"title":"ASE 頻譜：量測與判別","titleEn":"ASE spectrum: measurement and diagnosis","objective":"以「ASE 頻譜」區分機制並作出有證據的驗收決定，交付可重算且列明邊界的工程紀錄。","objectiveEn":"Discriminate mechanisms and make an evidence-based acceptance decision for ase spectrum, with reproducible calculations and stated boundaries.","instruction":"保留上一作業的模型，現在檢驗它是否足以解釋觀察。量測有無訊號兩種光譜，以相同解析頻寬估计 ASE 底噪。 記錄原始量、單位、基準與重複量測差異；以支持及否定各一項證據比較「放大自發輻射增加輸出功率但不等於有用訊號，頻譜積分需要解析頻寬。」與錯誤假說「所有輸入功率都保持相同小訊號增益。」，最後提出放行、重測或修模決定。","instructionEn":"Retain the previous model and test whether it explains the observations. Measure spectra with and without signal and estimate ASE at identical resolution bandwidth. Record raw quantities, units, reference conditions and repeatability. Use supporting and falsifying evidence to compare \"Amplified spontaneous emission adds output power but not useful signal; spectral integration requires resolution bandwidth.\" against the incorrect hypothesis \"Small-signal gain holds at every input power.\"; decide whether to accept, repeat or revise the model.","observation":"量測有無訊號兩種光譜，以相同解析頻寬估计 ASE 底噪。","observationEn":"Measure spectra with and without signal and estimate ASE at identical resolution bandwidth.","failure":"須排除的錯誤假說：所有輸入功率都保持相同小訊號增益。 若觀察不支持預測，先核對基準與單位，再依本步判別量測定位原因；不能只調參到曲線相合。","failureEn":"Incorrect hypothesis to reject: Small-signal gain holds at every input power. If observations disagree, first check references and units, then use this step's discriminating measurement; do not simply tune parameters until curves agree.","check":"提交ASE 頻譜的量測判別表：量測有無訊號兩種光譜，以相同解析頻寬估计 ASE 底噪。 附上基準、重複性或不確定度，及不能由本資料判定的結論。","checkEn":"Submit a measurement-discrimination table for ase spectrum: Measure spectra with and without signal and estimate ASE at identical resolution bandwidth. Include the reference, repeatability or uncertainty, and conclusions the data cannot support.","knowledge":[{"id":"a173-v9-14-k1","title":"本單元物理機制","titleEn":"Unit mechanism","text":"放大自發輻射增加輸出功率但不等於有用訊號，頻譜積分需要解析頻寬。","textEn":"Amplified spontaneous emission adds output power but not useful signal; spectral integration requires resolution bandwidth.","sourceIds":["v9c-soaexperiment","v9c-mprint"]},{"id":"a173-v9-14-k2","title":"獨立驗證與證據","titleEn":"Independent verification and evidence","text":"量測有無訊號兩種光譜，以相同解析頻寬估计 ASE 底噪。","textEn":"Measure spectra with and without signal and estimate ASE at identical resolution bandwidth.","sourceIds":["v9c-soaexperiment","v9c-mprint"]},{"id":"a173-v9-14-k3","title":"量化模型與適用邊界","titleEn":"Quantitative model and validity boundary","text":"GdB=10log10(Psignal,out/Psignal,in)，需扣除 ASE 並固定參考面。 未納入增益飽和、偏振及溫度變化；總光功率不等於訊號功率。","textEn":"GdB=10log10(Psignal,out/Psignal,in), with ASE removed and reference planes fixed. Saturation, polarization and temperature changes are excluded; total optical power is not signal power.","sourceIds":["v9c-soaexperiment","v9c-mprint"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要審查「ASE 頻譜」，哪項主張或驗證方法有根據？","questionEn":"Which claim or verification is justified when reviewing ase spectrum?","options":["ASE 全部是有用的調變訊號。","量測有無訊號兩種光譜，以相同解析頻寬估计 ASE 底噪。","所有輸入功率都保持相同小訊號增益。"],"optionsEn":["All ASE is useful modulated signal.","Measure spectra with and without signal and estimate ASE at identical resolution bandwidth.","Small-signal gain holds at every input power."],"answer":1,"explanation":"放大自發輻射增加輸出功率但不等於有用訊號，頻譜積分需要解析頻寬。 量測有無訊號兩種光譜，以相同解析頻寬估计 ASE 底噪。","explanationEn":"Amplified spontaneous emission adds output power but not useful signal; spectral integration requires resolution bandwidth. Measure spectra with and without signal and estimate ASE at identical resolution bandwidth."}},{"id":"a173-v9-15","order":3,"sequence":15,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9c-soaexperiment","v9c-mprint"],"prerequisiteIds":["a173-v9-14"],"title":"多波長增益競爭：模型與設計","titleEn":"Wavelength gain competition: model and design","objective":"以「多波長增益競爭」建立可檢驗的物理模型，交付可重算且列明邊界的工程紀錄。","objectiveEn":"Build a falsifiable physical model for wavelength gain competition, with reproducible calculations and stated boundaries.","instruction":"先以師傅示意確認「多波長增益競爭」的輸入、輸出與座標，再在學徒工作台完成對應元件或資料流的排列。多通道共用載子庫，單一強通道可能壓低其他通道增益。 用本單元的變數畫出至少兩種設計狀態，說明它們在「加入或移除一個強通道並觀察其他通道功率與雜訊。」的驗證中應有何差異；把待量測參數另列，不以動畫位置當成實際公差。","instructionEn":"Use the mentor view to identify the inputs, outputs and coordinates for wavelength gain competition, then arrange the corresponding components or data flow in the apprentice workspace. WDM channels share a carrier reservoir; one strong channel can suppress others. Draw at least two design states using this unit's variables and predict how the following verification distinguishes them: Add or remove one strong channel and monitor the others' power and noise. List unmeasured parameters separately; animation positions are not manufacturing tolerances.","observation":"加入或移除一個強通道並觀察其他通道功率與雜訊。","observationEn":"Add or remove one strong channel and monitor the others' power and noise.","failure":"須排除的錯誤假說：所有輸入功率都保持相同小訊號增益。 若觀察不支持預測，先核對基準與單位，再依本步判別量測定位原因；不能只調參到曲線相合。","failureEn":"Incorrect hypothesis to reject: Small-signal gain holds at every input power. If observations disagree, first check references and units, then use this step's discriminating measurement; do not simply tune parameters until curves agree.","check":"提交多波長增益競爭的兩狀態模型、變數表，以及能由「加入或移除一個強通道並觀察其他通道功率與雜訊。」反駁模型的預測。","checkEn":"Submit two model states and a variable table for wavelength gain competition, plus a falsifiable prediction using: Add or remove one strong channel and monitor the others' power and noise.","knowledge":[{"id":"a173-v9-15-k1","title":"本單元物理機制","titleEn":"Unit mechanism","text":"多通道共用載子庫，單一強通道可能壓低其他通道增益。","textEn":"WDM channels share a carrier reservoir; one strong channel can suppress others.","sourceIds":["v9c-soaexperiment","v9c-mprint"]},{"id":"a173-v9-15-k2","title":"獨立驗證與證據","titleEn":"Independent verification and evidence","text":"加入或移除一個強通道並觀察其他通道功率與雜訊。","textEn":"Add or remove one strong channel and monitor the others' power and noise.","sourceIds":["v9c-soaexperiment","v9c-mprint"]},{"id":"a173-v9-15-k3","title":"量化模型與適用邊界","titleEn":"Quantitative model and validity boundary","text":"GdB=10log10(Psignal,out/Psignal,in)，需扣除 ASE 並固定參考面。 未納入增益飽和、偏振及溫度變化；總光功率不等於訊號功率。","textEn":"GdB=10log10(Psignal,out/Psignal,in), with ASE removed and reference planes fixed. Saturation, polarization and temperature changes are excluded; total optical power is not signal power.","sourceIds":["v9c-soaexperiment","v9c-mprint"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要審查「多波長增益競爭」，哪項主張或驗證方法有根據？","questionEn":"Which claim or verification is justified when reviewing wavelength gain competition?","options":["所有輸入功率都保持相同小訊號增益。","ASE 全部是有用的調變訊號。","多通道共用載子庫，單一強通道可能壓低其他通道增益。"],"optionsEn":["Small-signal gain holds at every input power.","All ASE is useful modulated signal.","WDM channels share a carrier reservoir; one strong channel can suppress others."],"answer":2,"explanation":"多通道共用載子庫，單一強通道可能壓低其他通道增益。 加入或移除一個強通道並觀察其他通道功率與雜訊。","explanationEn":"WDM channels share a carrier reservoir; one strong channel can suppress others. Add or remove one strong channel and monitor the others' power and noise."}},{"id":"a173-v9-16","order":4,"sequence":16,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9c-soaexperiment","v9c-mprint"],"prerequisiteIds":["a173-v9-15"],"title":"多波長增益競爭：量測與判別","titleEn":"Wavelength gain competition: measurement and diagnosis","objective":"以「多波長增益競爭」區分機制並作出有證據的驗收決定，交付可重算且列明邊界的工程紀錄。","objectiveEn":"Discriminate mechanisms and make an evidence-based acceptance decision for wavelength gain competition, with reproducible calculations and stated boundaries.","instruction":"保留上一作業的模型，現在檢驗它是否足以解釋觀察。加入或移除一個強通道並觀察其他通道功率與雜訊。 記錄原始量、單位、基準與重複量測差異；以支持及否定各一項證據比較「多通道共用載子庫，單一強通道可能壓低其他通道增益。」與錯誤假說「ASE 全部是有用的調變訊號。」，最後提出放行、重測或修模決定。","instructionEn":"Retain the previous model and test whether it explains the observations. Add or remove one strong channel and monitor the others' power and noise. Record raw quantities, units, reference conditions and repeatability. Use supporting and falsifying evidence to compare \"WDM channels share a carrier reservoir; one strong channel can suppress others.\" against the incorrect hypothesis \"All ASE is useful modulated signal.\"; decide whether to accept, repeat or revise the model.","observation":"加入或移除一個強通道並觀察其他通道功率與雜訊。","observationEn":"Add or remove one strong channel and monitor the others' power and noise.","failure":"須排除的錯誤假說：ASE 全部是有用的調變訊號。 若觀察不支持預測，先核對基準與單位，再依本步判別量測定位原因；不能只調參到曲線相合。","failureEn":"Incorrect hypothesis to reject: All ASE is useful modulated signal. If observations disagree, first check references and units, then use this step's discriminating measurement; do not simply tune parameters until curves agree.","check":"提交多波長增益競爭的量測判別表：加入或移除一個強通道並觀察其他通道功率與雜訊。 附上基準、重複性或不確定度，及不能由本資料判定的結論。","checkEn":"Submit a measurement-discrimination table for wavelength gain competition: Add or remove one strong channel and monitor the others' power and noise. Include the reference, repeatability or uncertainty, and conclusions the data cannot support.","knowledge":[{"id":"a173-v9-16-k1","title":"本單元物理機制","titleEn":"Unit mechanism","text":"多通道共用載子庫，單一強通道可能壓低其他通道增益。","textEn":"WDM channels share a carrier reservoir; one strong channel can suppress others.","sourceIds":["v9c-soaexperiment","v9c-mprint"]},{"id":"a173-v9-16-k2","title":"獨立驗證與證據","titleEn":"Independent verification and evidence","text":"加入或移除一個強通道並觀察其他通道功率與雜訊。","textEn":"Add or remove one strong channel and monitor the others' power and noise.","sourceIds":["v9c-soaexperiment","v9c-mprint"]},{"id":"a173-v9-16-k3","title":"量化模型與適用邊界","titleEn":"Quantitative model and validity boundary","text":"GdB=10log10(Psignal,out/Psignal,in)，需扣除 ASE 並固定參考面。 未納入增益飽和、偏振及溫度變化；總光功率不等於訊號功率。","textEn":"GdB=10log10(Psignal,out/Psignal,in), with ASE removed and reference planes fixed. Saturation, polarization and temperature changes are excluded; total optical power is not signal power.","sourceIds":["v9c-soaexperiment","v9c-mprint"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要審查「多波長增益競爭」，哪項主張或驗證方法有根據？","questionEn":"Which claim or verification is justified when reviewing wavelength gain competition?","options":["加入或移除一個強通道並觀察其他通道功率與雜訊。","ASE 全部是有用的調變訊號。","補回功率就能完全補回 OSNR。"],"optionsEn":["Add or remove one strong channel and monitor the others' power and noise.","All ASE is useful modulated signal.","Restoring power fully restores OSNR."],"answer":0,"explanation":"多通道共用載子庫，單一強通道可能壓低其他通道增益。 加入或移除一個強通道並觀察其他通道功率與雜訊。","explanationEn":"WDM channels share a carrier reservoir; one strong channel can suppress others. Add or remove one strong channel and monitor the others' power and noise."}},{"id":"a173-v9-17","order":5,"sequence":17,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9c-soaexperiment","v9c-mprint"],"prerequisiteIds":["a173-v9-16"],"title":"瞬態增益恢復：模型與設計","titleEn":"Transient gain recovery: model and design","objective":"以「瞬態增益恢復」建立可檢驗的物理模型，交付可重算且列明邊界的工程紀錄。","objectiveEn":"Build a falsifiable physical model for transient gain recovery, with reproducible calculations and stated boundaries.","instruction":"先以師傅示意確認「瞬態增益恢復」的輸入、輸出與座標，再在學徒工作台完成對應元件或資料流的排列。載子恢復使增益具記憶性，長串連續符號可能引起圖樣相關失真。 用本單元的變數畫出至少兩種設計狀態，說明它們在「比較相同平均功率但不同符號圖樣的眼圖與功率暫態。」的驗證中應有何差異；把待量測參數另列，不以動畫位置當成實際公差。","instructionEn":"Use the mentor view to identify the inputs, outputs and coordinates for transient gain recovery, then arrange the corresponding components or data flow in the apprentice workspace. Carrier recovery gives gain memory, allowing pattern-dependent distortion. Draw at least two design states using this unit's variables and predict how the following verification distinguishes them: Compare eye diagrams and power transients for patterns with equal mean power. List unmeasured parameters separately; animation positions are not manufacturing tolerances.","observation":"比較相同平均功率但不同符號圖樣的眼圖與功率暫態。","observationEn":"Compare eye diagrams and power transients for patterns with equal mean power.","failure":"須排除的錯誤假說：ASE 全部是有用的調變訊號。 若觀察不支持預測，先核對基準與單位，再依本步判別量測定位原因；不能只調參到曲線相合。","failureEn":"Incorrect hypothesis to reject: All ASE is useful modulated signal. If observations disagree, first check references and units, then use this step's discriminating measurement; do not simply tune parameters until curves agree.","check":"提交瞬態增益恢復的兩狀態模型、變數表，以及能由「比較相同平均功率但不同符號圖樣的眼圖與功率暫態。」反駁模型的預測。","checkEn":"Submit two model states and a variable table for transient gain recovery, plus a falsifiable prediction using: Compare eye diagrams and power transients for patterns with equal mean power.","knowledge":[{"id":"a173-v9-17-k1","title":"本單元物理機制","titleEn":"Unit mechanism","text":"載子恢復使增益具記憶性，長串連續符號可能引起圖樣相關失真。","textEn":"Carrier recovery gives gain memory, allowing pattern-dependent distortion.","sourceIds":["v9c-soaexperiment","v9c-mprint"]},{"id":"a173-v9-17-k2","title":"獨立驗證與證據","titleEn":"Independent verification and evidence","text":"比較相同平均功率但不同符號圖樣的眼圖與功率暫態。","textEn":"Compare eye diagrams and power transients for patterns with equal mean power.","sourceIds":["v9c-soaexperiment","v9c-mprint"]},{"id":"a173-v9-17-k3","title":"量化模型與適用邊界","titleEn":"Quantitative model and validity boundary","text":"GdB=10log10(Psignal,out/Psignal,in)，需扣除 ASE 並固定參考面。 未納入增益飽和、偏振及溫度變化；總光功率不等於訊號功率。","textEn":"GdB=10log10(Psignal,out/Psignal,in), with ASE removed and reference planes fixed. Saturation, polarization and temperature changes are excluded; total optical power is not signal power.","sourceIds":["v9c-soaexperiment","v9c-mprint"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要審查「瞬態增益恢復」，哪項主張或驗證方法有根據？","questionEn":"Which claim or verification is justified when reviewing transient gain recovery?","options":["補回功率就能完全補回 OSNR。","載子恢復使增益具記憶性，長串連續符號可能引起圖樣相關失真。","ASE 全部是有用的調變訊號。"],"optionsEn":["Restoring power fully restores OSNR.","Carrier recovery gives gain memory, allowing pattern-dependent distortion.","All ASE is useful modulated signal."],"answer":1,"explanation":"載子恢復使增益具記憶性，長串連續符號可能引起圖樣相關失真。 比較相同平均功率但不同符號圖樣的眼圖與功率暫態。","explanationEn":"Carrier recovery gives gain memory, allowing pattern-dependent distortion. Compare eye diagrams and power transients for patterns with equal mean power."}},{"id":"a173-v9-18","order":6,"sequence":18,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9c-soaexperiment","v9c-mprint"],"prerequisiteIds":["a173-v9-17"],"title":"瞬態增益恢復：量測與判別","titleEn":"Transient gain recovery: measurement and diagnosis","objective":"以「瞬態增益恢復」區分機制並作出有證據的驗收決定，交付可重算且列明邊界的工程紀錄。","objectiveEn":"Discriminate mechanisms and make an evidence-based acceptance decision for transient gain recovery, with reproducible calculations and stated boundaries.","instruction":"保留上一作業的模型，現在檢驗它是否足以解釋觀察。比較相同平均功率但不同符號圖樣的眼圖與功率暫態。 記錄原始量、單位、基準與重複量測差異；以支持及否定各一項證據比較「載子恢復使增益具記憶性，長串連續符號可能引起圖樣相關失真。」與錯誤假說「補回功率就能完全補回 OSNR。」，最後提出放行、重測或修模決定。","instructionEn":"Retain the previous model and test whether it explains the observations. Compare eye diagrams and power transients for patterns with equal mean power. Record raw quantities, units, reference conditions and repeatability. Use supporting and falsifying evidence to compare \"Carrier recovery gives gain memory, allowing pattern-dependent distortion.\" against the incorrect hypothesis \"Restoring power fully restores OSNR.\"; decide whether to accept, repeat or revise the model.","observation":"比較相同平均功率但不同符號圖樣的眼圖與功率暫態。","observationEn":"Compare eye diagrams and power transients for patterns with equal mean power.","failure":"須排除的錯誤假說：補回功率就能完全補回 OSNR。 若觀察不支持預測，先核對基準與單位，再依本步判別量測定位原因；不能只調參到曲線相合。","failureEn":"Incorrect hypothesis to reject: Restoring power fully restores OSNR. If observations disagree, first check references and units, then use this step's discriminating measurement; do not simply tune parameters until curves agree.","check":"提交瞬態增益恢復的量測判別表：比較相同平均功率但不同符號圖樣的眼圖與功率暫態。 附上基準、重複性或不確定度，及不能由本資料判定的結論。","checkEn":"Submit a measurement-discrimination table for transient gain recovery: Compare eye diagrams and power transients for patterns with equal mean power. Include the reference, repeatability or uncertainty, and conclusions the data cannot support.","knowledge":[{"id":"a173-v9-18-k1","title":"本單元物理機制","titleEn":"Unit mechanism","text":"載子恢復使增益具記憶性，長串連續符號可能引起圖樣相關失真。","textEn":"Carrier recovery gives gain memory, allowing pattern-dependent distortion.","sourceIds":["v9c-soaexperiment","v9c-mprint"]},{"id":"a173-v9-18-k2","title":"獨立驗證與證據","titleEn":"Independent verification and evidence","text":"比較相同平均功率但不同符號圖樣的眼圖與功率暫態。","textEn":"Compare eye diagrams and power transients for patterns with equal mean power.","sourceIds":["v9c-soaexperiment","v9c-mprint"]},{"id":"a173-v9-18-k3","title":"量化模型與適用邊界","titleEn":"Quantitative model and validity boundary","text":"GdB=10log10(Psignal,out/Psignal,in)，需扣除 ASE 並固定參考面。 未納入增益飽和、偏振及溫度變化；總光功率不等於訊號功率。","textEn":"GdB=10log10(Psignal,out/Psignal,in), with ASE removed and reference planes fixed. Saturation, polarization and temperature changes are excluded; total optical power is not signal power.","sourceIds":["v9c-soaexperiment","v9c-mprint"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要審查「瞬態增益恢復」，哪項主張或驗證方法有根據？","questionEn":"Which claim or verification is justified when reviewing transient gain recovery?","options":["補回功率就能完全補回 OSNR。","所有輸入功率都保持相同小訊號增益。","比較相同平均功率但不同符號圖樣的眼圖與功率暫態。"],"optionsEn":["Restoring power fully restores OSNR.","Small-signal gain holds at every input power.","Compare eye diagrams and power transients for patterns with equal mean power."],"answer":2,"explanation":"載子恢復使增益具記憶性，長串連續符號可能引起圖樣相關失真。 比較相同平均功率但不同符號圖樣的眼圖與功率暫態。","explanationEn":"Carrier recovery gives gain memory, allowing pattern-dependent distortion. Compare eye diagrams and power transients for patterns with equal mean power."}}]},{"id":"a173-stage04","order":4,"title":"熱與驗收","titleEn":"Heat and acceptance","description":"以三個技術單元完成「熱與驗收」的模型與驗證，六項作業各自留存交付物。","descriptionEn":"Three technical units address Heat and acceptance through six separately saved modeling and verification work packages.","steps":[{"id":"a173-v9-19","order":1,"sequence":19,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9c-soaexperiment","v9c-mprint"],"prerequisiteIds":["a173-v9-18"],"title":"電流與熱：模型與設計","titleEn":"Current and heat: model and design","objective":"以「電流與熱」建立可檢驗的物理模型，交付可重算且列明邊界的工程紀錄。","objectiveEn":"Build a falsifiable physical model for current and heat, with reproducible calculations and stated boundaries.","instruction":"先以師傅示意確認「電流與熱」的輸入、輸出與座標，再在學徒工作台完成對應元件或資料流的排列。增加電流不保證線性增加淨增益，額外自熱也改變波段與飽和。 用本單元的變數畫出至少兩種設計狀態，說明它們在「記錄 I-V、溫度和增益三者，分辨電流效果與熱回授。」的驗證中應有何差異；把待量測參數另列，不以動畫位置當成實際公差。","instructionEn":"Use the mentor view to identify the inputs, outputs and coordinates for current and heat, then arrange the corresponding components or data flow in the apprentice workspace. More current need not linearly increase net gain; heating shifts spectrum and saturation. Draw at least two design states using this unit's variables and predict how the following verification distinguishes them: Record I-V, temperature and gain together to separate current effects from thermal feedback. List unmeasured parameters separately; animation positions are not manufacturing tolerances.","observation":"記錄 I-V、溫度和增益三者，分辨電流效果與熱回授。","observationEn":"Record I-V, temperature and gain together to separate current effects from thermal feedback.","failure":"須排除的錯誤假說：補回功率就能完全補回 OSNR。 若觀察不支持預測，先核對基準與單位，再依本步判別量測定位原因；不能只調參到曲線相合。","failureEn":"Incorrect hypothesis to reject: Restoring power fully restores OSNR. If observations disagree, first check references and units, then use this step's discriminating measurement; do not simply tune parameters until curves agree.","check":"提交電流與熱的兩狀態模型、變數表，以及能由「記錄 I-V、溫度和增益三者，分辨電流效果與熱回授。」反駁模型的預測。","checkEn":"Submit two model states and a variable table for current and heat, plus a falsifiable prediction using: Record I-V, temperature and gain together to separate current effects from thermal feedback.","knowledge":[{"id":"a173-v9-19-k1","title":"本單元物理機制","titleEn":"Unit mechanism","text":"增加電流不保證線性增加淨增益，額外自熱也改變波段與飽和。","textEn":"More current need not linearly increase net gain; heating shifts spectrum and saturation.","sourceIds":["v9c-soaexperiment","v9c-mprint"]},{"id":"a173-v9-19-k2","title":"獨立驗證與證據","titleEn":"Independent verification and evidence","text":"記錄 I-V、溫度和增益三者，分辨電流效果與熱回授。","textEn":"Record I-V, temperature and gain together to separate current effects from thermal feedback.","sourceIds":["v9c-soaexperiment","v9c-mprint"]},{"id":"a173-v9-19-k3","title":"量化模型與適用邊界","titleEn":"Quantitative model and validity boundary","text":"GdB=10log10(Psignal,out/Psignal,in)，需扣除 ASE 並固定參考面。 未納入增益飽和、偏振及溫度變化；總光功率不等於訊號功率。","textEn":"GdB=10log10(Psignal,out/Psignal,in), with ASE removed and reference planes fixed. Saturation, polarization and temperature changes are excluded; total optical power is not signal power.","sourceIds":["v9c-soaexperiment","v9c-mprint"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要審查「電流與熱」，哪項主張或驗證方法有根據？","questionEn":"Which claim or verification is justified when reviewing current and heat?","options":["增加電流不保證線性增加淨增益，額外自熱也改變波段與飽和。","補回功率就能完全補回 OSNR。","所有輸入功率都保持相同小訊號增益。"],"optionsEn":["More current need not linearly increase net gain; heating shifts spectrum and saturation.","Restoring power fully restores OSNR.","Small-signal gain holds at every input power."],"answer":0,"explanation":"增加電流不保證線性增加淨增益，額外自熱也改變波段與飽和。 記錄 I-V、溫度和增益三者，分辨電流效果與熱回授。","explanationEn":"More current need not linearly increase net gain; heating shifts spectrum and saturation. Record I-V, temperature and gain together to separate current effects from thermal feedback."}},{"id":"a173-v9-20","order":2,"sequence":20,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9c-soaexperiment","v9c-mprint"],"prerequisiteIds":["a173-v9-19"],"title":"電流與熱：量測與判別","titleEn":"Current and heat: measurement and diagnosis","objective":"以「電流與熱」區分機制並作出有證據的驗收決定，交付可重算且列明邊界的工程紀錄。","objectiveEn":"Discriminate mechanisms and make an evidence-based acceptance decision for current and heat, with reproducible calculations and stated boundaries.","instruction":"保留上一作業的模型，現在檢驗它是否足以解釋觀察。記錄 I-V、溫度和增益三者，分辨電流效果與熱回授。 記錄原始量、單位、基準與重複量測差異；以支持及否定各一項證據比較「增加電流不保證線性增加淨增益，額外自熱也改變波段與飽和。」與錯誤假說「所有輸入功率都保持相同小訊號增益。」，最後提出放行、重測或修模決定。","instructionEn":"Retain the previous model and test whether it explains the observations. Record I-V, temperature and gain together to separate current effects from thermal feedback. Record raw quantities, units, reference conditions and repeatability. Use supporting and falsifying evidence to compare \"More current need not linearly increase net gain; heating shifts spectrum and saturation.\" against the incorrect hypothesis \"Small-signal gain holds at every input power.\"; decide whether to accept, repeat or revise the model.","observation":"記錄 I-V、溫度和增益三者，分辨電流效果與熱回授。","observationEn":"Record I-V, temperature and gain together to separate current effects from thermal feedback.","failure":"須排除的錯誤假說：所有輸入功率都保持相同小訊號增益。 若觀察不支持預測，先核對基準與單位，再依本步判別量測定位原因；不能只調參到曲線相合。","failureEn":"Incorrect hypothesis to reject: Small-signal gain holds at every input power. If observations disagree, first check references and units, then use this step's discriminating measurement; do not simply tune parameters until curves agree.","check":"提交電流與熱的量測判別表：記錄 I-V、溫度和增益三者，分辨電流效果與熱回授。 附上基準、重複性或不確定度，及不能由本資料判定的結論。","checkEn":"Submit a measurement-discrimination table for current and heat: Record I-V, temperature and gain together to separate current effects from thermal feedback. Include the reference, repeatability or uncertainty, and conclusions the data cannot support.","knowledge":[{"id":"a173-v9-20-k1","title":"本單元物理機制","titleEn":"Unit mechanism","text":"增加電流不保證線性增加淨增益，額外自熱也改變波段與飽和。","textEn":"More current need not linearly increase net gain; heating shifts spectrum and saturation.","sourceIds":["v9c-soaexperiment","v9c-mprint"]},{"id":"a173-v9-20-k2","title":"獨立驗證與證據","titleEn":"Independent verification and evidence","text":"記錄 I-V、溫度和增益三者，分辨電流效果與熱回授。","textEn":"Record I-V, temperature and gain together to separate current effects from thermal feedback.","sourceIds":["v9c-soaexperiment","v9c-mprint"]},{"id":"a173-v9-20-k3","title":"量化模型與適用邊界","titleEn":"Quantitative model and validity boundary","text":"GdB=10log10(Psignal,out/Psignal,in)，需扣除 ASE 並固定參考面。 未納入增益飽和、偏振及溫度變化；總光功率不等於訊號功率。","textEn":"GdB=10log10(Psignal,out/Psignal,in), with ASE removed and reference planes fixed. Saturation, polarization and temperature changes are excluded; total optical power is not signal power.","sourceIds":["v9c-soaexperiment","v9c-mprint"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要審查「電流與熱」，哪項主張或驗證方法有根據？","questionEn":"Which claim or verification is justified when reviewing current and heat?","options":["ASE 全部是有用的調變訊號。","記錄 I-V、溫度和增益三者，分辨電流效果與熱回授。","所有輸入功率都保持相同小訊號增益。"],"optionsEn":["All ASE is useful modulated signal.","Record I-V, temperature and gain together to separate current effects from thermal feedback.","Small-signal gain holds at every input power."],"answer":1,"explanation":"增加電流不保證線性增加淨增益，額外自熱也改變波段與飽和。 記錄 I-V、溫度和增益三者，分辨電流效果與熱回授。","explanationEn":"More current need not linearly increase net gain; heating shifts spectrum and saturation. Record I-V, temperature and gain together to separate current effects from thermal feedback."}},{"id":"a173-v9-21","order":3,"sequence":21,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9c-soaexperiment","v9c-mprint"],"prerequisiteIds":["a173-v9-20"],"title":"雜訊串接：模型與設計","titleEn":"Noise cascading: model and design","objective":"以「雜訊串接」建立可檢驗的物理模型，交付可重算且列明邊界的工程紀錄。","objectiveEn":"Build a falsifiable physical model for noise cascading, with reproducible calculations and stated boundaries.","instruction":"先以師傅示意確認「雜訊串接」的輸入、輸出與座標，再在學徒工作台完成對應元件或資料流的排列。補回插損不會恢復被破壞的訊雜比；SOA 本身還會加入 ASE。 用本單元的變數畫出至少兩種設計狀態，說明它們在「比較放大前後 OSNR，在相同量測頻寬下判讀。」的驗證中應有何差異；把待量測參數另列，不以動畫位置當成實際公差。","instructionEn":"Use the mentor view to identify the inputs, outputs and coordinates for noise cascading, then arrange the corresponding components or data flow in the apprentice workspace. Compensating loss does not restore lost signal-to-noise ratio; the SOA also adds ASE. Draw at least two design states using this unit's variables and predict how the following verification distinguishes them: Compare pre/post-amplifier OSNR using the same measurement bandwidth. List unmeasured parameters separately; animation positions are not manufacturing tolerances.","observation":"比較放大前後 OSNR，在相同量測頻寬下判讀。","observationEn":"Compare pre/post-amplifier OSNR using the same measurement bandwidth.","failure":"須排除的錯誤假說：所有輸入功率都保持相同小訊號增益。 若觀察不支持預測，先核對基準與單位，再依本步判別量測定位原因；不能只調參到曲線相合。","failureEn":"Incorrect hypothesis to reject: Small-signal gain holds at every input power. If observations disagree, first check references and units, then use this step's discriminating measurement; do not simply tune parameters until curves agree.","check":"提交雜訊串接的兩狀態模型、變數表，以及能由「比較放大前後 OSNR，在相同量測頻寬下判讀。」反駁模型的預測。","checkEn":"Submit two model states and a variable table for noise cascading, plus a falsifiable prediction using: Compare pre/post-amplifier OSNR using the same measurement bandwidth.","knowledge":[{"id":"a173-v9-21-k1","title":"本單元物理機制","titleEn":"Unit mechanism","text":"補回插損不會恢復被破壞的訊雜比；SOA 本身還會加入 ASE。","textEn":"Compensating loss does not restore lost signal-to-noise ratio; the SOA also adds ASE.","sourceIds":["v9c-soaexperiment","v9c-mprint"]},{"id":"a173-v9-21-k2","title":"獨立驗證與證據","titleEn":"Independent verification and evidence","text":"比較放大前後 OSNR，在相同量測頻寬下判讀。","textEn":"Compare pre/post-amplifier OSNR using the same measurement bandwidth.","sourceIds":["v9c-soaexperiment","v9c-mprint"]},{"id":"a173-v9-21-k3","title":"量化模型與適用邊界","titleEn":"Quantitative model and validity boundary","text":"GdB=10log10(Psignal,out/Psignal,in)，需扣除 ASE 並固定參考面。 未納入增益飽和、偏振及溫度變化；總光功率不等於訊號功率。","textEn":"GdB=10log10(Psignal,out/Psignal,in), with ASE removed and reference planes fixed. Saturation, polarization and temperature changes are excluded; total optical power is not signal power.","sourceIds":["v9c-soaexperiment","v9c-mprint"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要審查「雜訊串接」，哪項主張或驗證方法有根據？","questionEn":"Which claim or verification is justified when reviewing noise cascading?","options":["所有輸入功率都保持相同小訊號增益。","ASE 全部是有用的調變訊號。","補回插損不會恢復被破壞的訊雜比；SOA 本身還會加入 ASE。"],"optionsEn":["Small-signal gain holds at every input power.","All ASE is useful modulated signal.","Compensating loss does not restore lost signal-to-noise ratio; the SOA also adds ASE."],"answer":2,"explanation":"補回插損不會恢復被破壞的訊雜比；SOA 本身還會加入 ASE。 比較放大前後 OSNR，在相同量測頻寬下判讀。","explanationEn":"Compensating loss does not restore lost signal-to-noise ratio; the SOA also adds ASE. Compare pre/post-amplifier OSNR using the same measurement bandwidth."}},{"id":"a173-v9-22","order":4,"sequence":22,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9c-soaexperiment","v9c-mprint"],"prerequisiteIds":["a173-v9-21"],"title":"雜訊串接：量測與判別","titleEn":"Noise cascading: measurement and diagnosis","objective":"以「雜訊串接」區分機制並作出有證據的驗收決定，交付可重算且列明邊界的工程紀錄。","objectiveEn":"Discriminate mechanisms and make an evidence-based acceptance decision for noise cascading, with reproducible calculations and stated boundaries.","instruction":"保留上一作業的模型，現在檢驗它是否足以解釋觀察。比較放大前後 OSNR，在相同量測頻寬下判讀。 記錄原始量、單位、基準與重複量測差異；以支持及否定各一項證據比較「補回插損不會恢復被破壞的訊雜比；SOA 本身還會加入 ASE。」與錯誤假說「ASE 全部是有用的調變訊號。」，最後提出放行、重測或修模決定。","instructionEn":"Retain the previous model and test whether it explains the observations. Compare pre/post-amplifier OSNR using the same measurement bandwidth. Record raw quantities, units, reference conditions and repeatability. Use supporting and falsifying evidence to compare \"Compensating loss does not restore lost signal-to-noise ratio; the SOA also adds ASE.\" against the incorrect hypothesis \"All ASE is useful modulated signal.\"; decide whether to accept, repeat or revise the model.","observation":"比較放大前後 OSNR，在相同量測頻寬下判讀。","observationEn":"Compare pre/post-amplifier OSNR using the same measurement bandwidth.","failure":"須排除的錯誤假說：ASE 全部是有用的調變訊號。 若觀察不支持預測，先核對基準與單位，再依本步判別量測定位原因；不能只調參到曲線相合。","failureEn":"Incorrect hypothesis to reject: All ASE is useful modulated signal. If observations disagree, first check references and units, then use this step's discriminating measurement; do not simply tune parameters until curves agree.","check":"提交雜訊串接的量測判別表：比較放大前後 OSNR，在相同量測頻寬下判讀。 附上基準、重複性或不確定度，及不能由本資料判定的結論。","checkEn":"Submit a measurement-discrimination table for noise cascading: Compare pre/post-amplifier OSNR using the same measurement bandwidth. Include the reference, repeatability or uncertainty, and conclusions the data cannot support.","knowledge":[{"id":"a173-v9-22-k1","title":"本單元物理機制","titleEn":"Unit mechanism","text":"補回插損不會恢復被破壞的訊雜比；SOA 本身還會加入 ASE。","textEn":"Compensating loss does not restore lost signal-to-noise ratio; the SOA also adds ASE.","sourceIds":["v9c-soaexperiment","v9c-mprint"]},{"id":"a173-v9-22-k2","title":"獨立驗證與證據","titleEn":"Independent verification and evidence","text":"比較放大前後 OSNR，在相同量測頻寬下判讀。","textEn":"Compare pre/post-amplifier OSNR using the same measurement bandwidth.","sourceIds":["v9c-soaexperiment","v9c-mprint"]},{"id":"a173-v9-22-k3","title":"量化模型與適用邊界","titleEn":"Quantitative model and validity boundary","text":"GdB=10log10(Psignal,out/Psignal,in)，需扣除 ASE 並固定參考面。 未納入增益飽和、偏振及溫度變化；總光功率不等於訊號功率。","textEn":"GdB=10log10(Psignal,out/Psignal,in), with ASE removed and reference planes fixed. Saturation, polarization and temperature changes are excluded; total optical power is not signal power.","sourceIds":["v9c-soaexperiment","v9c-mprint"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要審查「雜訊串接」，哪項主張或驗證方法有根據？","questionEn":"Which claim or verification is justified when reviewing noise cascading?","options":["比較放大前後 OSNR，在相同量測頻寬下判讀。","ASE 全部是有用的調變訊號。","補回功率就能完全補回 OSNR。"],"optionsEn":["Compare pre/post-amplifier OSNR using the same measurement bandwidth.","All ASE is useful modulated signal.","Restoring power fully restores OSNR."],"answer":0,"explanation":"補回插損不會恢復被破壞的訊雜比；SOA 本身還會加入 ASE。 比較放大前後 OSNR，在相同量測頻寬下判讀。","explanationEn":"Compensating loss does not restore lost signal-to-noise ratio; the SOA also adds ASE. Compare pre/post-amplifier OSNR using the same measurement bandwidth."}},{"id":"a173-v9-23","order":5,"sequence":23,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9c-soaexperiment","v9c-mprint"],"prerequisiteIds":["a173-v9-22"],"title":"系統驗收：模型與設計","titleEn":"System acceptance: model and design","objective":"以「系統驗收」建立可檢驗的物理模型，交付可重算且列明邊界的工程紀錄。","objectiveEn":"Build a falsifiable physical model for system acceptance, with reproducible calculations and stated boundaries.","instruction":"先以師傅示意確認「系統驗收」的輸入、輸出與座標，再在學徒工作台完成對應元件或資料流的排列。開關網路的淨增益、串擾與總功耗要一起驗收，不能只列零淨插損。 用本單元的變數畫出至少兩種設計狀態，說明它們在「建立不同路由與通道負載下的增益、BER 及熱矩陣。」的驗證中應有何差異；把待量測參數另列，不以動畫位置當成實際公差。","instructionEn":"Use the mentor view to identify the inputs, outputs and coordinates for system acceptance, then arrange the corresponding components or data flow in the apprentice workspace. Accept switch-network net gain, crosstalk and total power together, not only zero net loss. Draw at least two design states using this unit's variables and predict how the following verification distinguishes them: Build gain, BER and thermal matrices across routes and channel loads. List unmeasured parameters separately; animation positions are not manufacturing tolerances.","observation":"建立不同路由與通道負載下的增益、BER 及熱矩陣。","observationEn":"Build gain, BER and thermal matrices across routes and channel loads.","failure":"須排除的錯誤假說：ASE 全部是有用的調變訊號。 若觀察不支持預測，先核對基準與單位，再依本步判別量測定位原因；不能只調參到曲線相合。","failureEn":"Incorrect hypothesis to reject: All ASE is useful modulated signal. If observations disagree, first check references and units, then use this step's discriminating measurement; do not simply tune parameters until curves agree.","check":"提交系統驗收的兩狀態模型、變數表，以及能由「建立不同路由與通道負載下的增益、BER 及熱矩陣。」反駁模型的預測。","checkEn":"Submit two model states and a variable table for system acceptance, plus a falsifiable prediction using: Build gain, BER and thermal matrices across routes and channel loads.","knowledge":[{"id":"a173-v9-23-k1","title":"本單元物理機制","titleEn":"Unit mechanism","text":"開關網路的淨增益、串擾與總功耗要一起驗收，不能只列零淨插損。","textEn":"Accept switch-network net gain, crosstalk and total power together, not only zero net loss.","sourceIds":["v9c-soaexperiment","v9c-mprint"]},{"id":"a173-v9-23-k2","title":"獨立驗證與證據","titleEn":"Independent verification and evidence","text":"建立不同路由與通道負載下的增益、BER 及熱矩陣。","textEn":"Build gain, BER and thermal matrices across routes and channel loads.","sourceIds":["v9c-soaexperiment","v9c-mprint"]},{"id":"a173-v9-23-k3","title":"量化模型與適用邊界","titleEn":"Quantitative model and validity boundary","text":"GdB=10log10(Psignal,out/Psignal,in)，需扣除 ASE 並固定參考面。 未納入增益飽和、偏振及溫度變化；總光功率不等於訊號功率。","textEn":"GdB=10log10(Psignal,out/Psignal,in), with ASE removed and reference planes fixed. Saturation, polarization and temperature changes are excluded; total optical power is not signal power.","sourceIds":["v9c-soaexperiment","v9c-mprint"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要審查「系統驗收」，哪項主張或驗證方法有根據？","questionEn":"Which claim or verification is justified when reviewing system acceptance?","options":["補回功率就能完全補回 OSNR。","開關網路的淨增益、串擾與總功耗要一起驗收，不能只列零淨插損。","ASE 全部是有用的調變訊號。"],"optionsEn":["Restoring power fully restores OSNR.","Accept switch-network net gain, crosstalk and total power together, not only zero net loss.","All ASE is useful modulated signal."],"answer":1,"explanation":"開關網路的淨增益、串擾與總功耗要一起驗收，不能只列零淨插損。 建立不同路由與通道負載下的增益、BER 及熱矩陣。","explanationEn":"Accept switch-network net gain, crosstalk and total power together, not only zero net loss. Build gain, BER and thermal matrices across routes and channel loads."}},{"id":"a173-v9-24","order":6,"sequence":24,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v9c-soaexperiment","v9c-mprint"],"prerequisiteIds":["a173-v9-23"],"title":"系統驗收：量測與判別","titleEn":"System acceptance: measurement and diagnosis","objective":"以「系統驗收」區分機制並作出有證據的驗收決定，交付可重算且列明邊界的工程紀錄。","objectiveEn":"Discriminate mechanisms and make an evidence-based acceptance decision for system acceptance, with reproducible calculations and stated boundaries.","instruction":"保留上一作業的模型，現在檢驗它是否足以解釋觀察。建立不同路由與通道負載下的增益、BER 及熱矩陣。 記錄原始量、單位、基準與重複量測差異；以支持及否定各一項證據比較「開關網路的淨增益、串擾與總功耗要一起驗收，不能只列零淨插損。」與錯誤假說「補回功率就能完全補回 OSNR。」，最後提出放行、重測或修模決定。","instructionEn":"Retain the previous model and test whether it explains the observations. Build gain, BER and thermal matrices across routes and channel loads. Record raw quantities, units, reference conditions and repeatability. Use supporting and falsifying evidence to compare \"Accept switch-network net gain, crosstalk and total power together, not only zero net loss.\" against the incorrect hypothesis \"Restoring power fully restores OSNR.\"; decide whether to accept, repeat or revise the model.","observation":"建立不同路由與通道負載下的增益、BER 及熱矩陣。","observationEn":"Build gain, BER and thermal matrices across routes and channel loads.","failure":"須排除的錯誤假說：補回功率就能完全補回 OSNR。 若觀察不支持預測，先核對基準與單位，再依本步判別量測定位原因；不能只調參到曲線相合。","failureEn":"Incorrect hypothesis to reject: Restoring power fully restores OSNR. If observations disagree, first check references and units, then use this step's discriminating measurement; do not simply tune parameters until curves agree.","check":"提交系統驗收的量測判別表：建立不同路由與通道負載下的增益、BER 及熱矩陣。 附上基準、重複性或不確定度，及不能由本資料判定的結論。","checkEn":"Submit a measurement-discrimination table for system acceptance: Build gain, BER and thermal matrices across routes and channel loads. Include the reference, repeatability or uncertainty, and conclusions the data cannot support.","knowledge":[{"id":"a173-v9-24-k1","title":"本單元物理機制","titleEn":"Unit mechanism","text":"開關網路的淨增益、串擾與總功耗要一起驗收，不能只列零淨插損。","textEn":"Accept switch-network net gain, crosstalk and total power together, not only zero net loss.","sourceIds":["v9c-soaexperiment","v9c-mprint"]},{"id":"a173-v9-24-k2","title":"獨立驗證與證據","titleEn":"Independent verification and evidence","text":"建立不同路由與通道負載下的增益、BER 及熱矩陣。","textEn":"Build gain, BER and thermal matrices across routes and channel loads.","sourceIds":["v9c-soaexperiment","v9c-mprint"]},{"id":"a173-v9-24-k3","title":"量化模型與適用邊界","titleEn":"Quantitative model and validity boundary","text":"GdB=10log10(Psignal,out/Psignal,in)，需扣除 ASE 並固定參考面。 未納入增益飽和、偏振及溫度變化；總光功率不等於訊號功率。","textEn":"GdB=10log10(Psignal,out/Psignal,in), with ASE removed and reference planes fixed. Saturation, polarization and temperature changes are excluded; total optical power is not signal power.","sourceIds":["v9c-soaexperiment","v9c-mprint"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要審查「系統驗收」，哪項主張或驗證方法有根據？","questionEn":"Which claim or verification is justified when reviewing system acceptance?","options":["補回功率就能完全補回 OSNR。","所有輸入功率都保持相同小訊號增益。","建立不同路由與通道負載下的增益、BER 及熱矩陣。"],"optionsEn":["Restoring power fully restores OSNR.","Small-signal gain holds at every input power.","Build gain, BER and thermal matrices across routes and channel loads."],"answer":2,"explanation":"開關網路的淨增益、串擾與總功耗要一起驗收，不能只列零淨插損。 建立不同路由與通道負載下的增益、BER 及熱矩陣。","explanationEn":"Accept switch-network net gain, crosstalk and total power together, not only zero net loss. Build gain, BER and thermal matrices across routes and channel loads."}}]}],"subcategoryTitle":"異質材料、雷射與光源","subcategoryTitleEn":"Heterogeneous materials, lasers and sources","photoId":"v9-laser-chip"}};
